1
00:00:12,599 --> 00:00:16,399
今晚——理查德把车甩出赛道，甩了两次！
Tonight -
Richard spins off the track. Twice!

2
00:00:16,399 --> 00:00:17,999
啊！
Agh!

3
00:00:17,999 --> 00:00:19,799
Jay Kay 想抢第一名。
Jay Kay tries to get to number one.

4
00:00:19,799 --> 00:00:22,119
德国和英国——哪个好？
And Germany or Britain -
which is best?

5
00:00:31,039 --> 00:00:32,639
谢谢，你好。
Thank you, hello.

6
00:00:32,639 --> 00:00:34,160
大家好，欢迎收看。
Hello and welcome.

7
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:35,960
非常感谢。
Thanks very much.

8
00:00:35,960 --> 00:00:38,159
现在……
Now...

9
00:00:38,159 --> 00:00:40,640
现在，在我们……
now, after our...

10
00:00:40,640 --> 00:00:45,280
我们最近去日本的旅行，我和子弹列车赛了一把，
our recent trip to Japan,
where I raced the Bullet Train,

11
00:00:45,280 --> 00:00:50,480
我多待了一天，去赛道上开了日产 GT‑R。
I stayed on for an extra day
to drive the Nissan GT-R
around the track.

12
00:00:50,480 --> 00:00:53,879
而詹姆斯则决定稍作停留，
James, on the other hand, decided
to stay on for a little while

13
00:00:53,879 --> 00:00:59,680
因为他想开一辆自称更贴近普通英国车主的车，
as he wanted to drive a car that
he claimed would be more relevant
to the average British motorist

14
00:00:59,680 --> 00:01:03,199
比起那辆涨价到五万英镑的达特桑。
than a jumped up £50,000 Datsun.

15
00:01:07,919 --> 00:01:12,040
现在，我相当有把握你们之前都没见过这种车。
Now, I'm fairly confident you
won't have seen one of these before.

16
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:15,800
准备好了吗？
Are you ready?

17
00:01:20,440 --> 00:01:22,240
它叫做 Orochi（欧罗奇）。
It's called the Orochi.

18
00:01:22,240 --> 00:01:27,040
它的外形灵感来自一条鱼、一条蛇，还有帕梅拉·安德森的嘴巴。
It's looks are based on a fish,
a snake and Pamela Anderson's mouth.

19
00:01:29,799 --> 00:01:31,999
我还挺喜欢的。
I rather like it.

20
00:01:31,999 --> 00:01:36,640
它卖四万四千英镑，产自一家叫 Mitsuoka（光冈）的公司。
It costs £44,000. It's made
by a company called Mitsuoka.

21
00:01:38,279 --> 00:01:43,439
你们大概也没听说过它们，但它们可是真正的日本造车厂。
You've probably never heard of them
either, but they are a proper
Japanese car maker.

22
00:01:43,439 --> 00:01:46,480
事实上，它们是日本第十大汽车制造商，
In fact, they're the tenth biggest
car maker in the country,

23
00:01:46,480 --> 00:01:51,440
排在丰田、日产、本田以及另外六家之后。
after Toyota, Nissan, Honda
and six others.

24
00:01:56,639 --> 00:02:02,200
光冈自己打造底盘、车身和内饰，
Mitsuoka makes the chassis, the body
and the interior all by itself,

25
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:05,680
但发动机——一台 3.3 升 V6——却是丰田提供的。
but the engine,
a 3.3 litre V6, comes from Toyota.

26
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:15,800
所以它长得像跑车，但真的像跑车吗？
So, it looks like a sports car,
but is it any good as one?

27
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:23,039
说实话，它不快，噪音也不大，坐起来却意外地舒适。
Well, it isn't very fast, it
doesn't make much noise and the
ride is surprisingly comfortable.

28
00:02:23,039 --> 00:02:26,999
也就是说，它的乘坐感受对超级跑车来说相当不错，
By which I mean the ride is
rather excellent for a supercar,

29
00:02:26,999 --> 00:02:29,680
所以显然，我觉得它挺适合我的。
so, obviously,
I think it suits me rather well.

30
00:02:29,680 --> 00:02:34,240
不过，哈蒙德和克拉克森可能还想继续逛逛别的车。
Although, Hammond and Clarkson might
like to continue to shop around.

31
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:40,559
但光冈还有另一款车，纸面上看更合我胃口。
But Mitsuoka makes another car,
which, on paper,
is even more up my street.

32
00:02:45,200 --> 00:02:48,599
这就是，它叫 Galue（加勒）。
Here it is,
and it's called the Galue.

33
00:02:48,599 --> 00:02:51,560
那位顶级社会评论员艾伦·帕特里奇，
That foremost social commentator,
Alan Partridge,

34
00:02:51,560 --> 00:02:55,199
曾说过雷克萨是日本的奔驰。
once said that the Lexus
is Japan's Mercedes Benz.

35
00:02:55,199 --> 00:03:00,239
如果这样的话，光冈 Galue 也许——但这只是我的直觉——
In which case, the Mitsuoka Galue
could be - but this is only a hunch -

36
00:03:00,239 --> 00:03:02,519
可以算是日本的劳斯莱斯。
Japan's Rolls Royce.

37
00:03:04,880 --> 00:03:11,200
不过价格相当友好，没那么劳斯莱斯贵，仅三万二千英镑。
But at a nice,
un-Rolls-Royce-ish price,
because it cost an agreeable £32,000.

38
00:03:12,839 --> 00:03:18,519
但长得像劳斯莱斯是一回事，开起来像劳斯莱斯可是完全另一番滋味。
But looking like a Rolls-Royce
is one thing - feeling like a
Rolls-Royce is completely different.

39
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:26,519
于是，为了验证真相，节目组安排我来一次贵宾专车试驾。
So, to find out whether it does or
not, the producers have arranged for
me to do a spot of VIP chauffeuring.

40
00:03:26,519 --> 00:03:28,800
不是他。
Not him.

41
00:03:28,800 --> 00:03:31,719
他们。
Them.

42
00:03:31,719 --> 00:03:36,920
是的，那位当地相扑选手和他的经纪人得送去参加比赛。
Yes, the local sumo wrestler and his
manager need taking to a tournament.

43
00:03:38,639 --> 00:03:39,800
喂，你好。
Konichiwa.

44
00:03:42,320 --> 00:03:44,599
我的日语已经说得精疲力竭。
That's exhausted my Japanese.

45
00:03:44,599 --> 00:03:48,959
好，回到日本版劳斯莱斯吧。
Right, back to the Japanese
Rolls-Royce.

46
00:03:48,959 --> 00:03:56,439
在Galue内部，光冈把那种正宗、老派的英伦豪车氛围给重新复制了。
Inside the Galue, Mitsuoka has
recreated the ambience of a proper,
old school, British luxury car.

47
00:03:56,439 --> 00:04:00,519
有点木头感，差不多。豪华真皮座椅。
There's some wood. Ish.
Plush leather seats.

48
00:04:00,519 --> 00:04:07,279
但是你看看——这块钟表跟新款劳斯莱斯幻影的那个简直一模一样，差不多。
But look at this - this clock
is exactly, roughly like the one
on the new Rolls-Royce Phantom.

49
00:04:07,279 --> 00:04:12,280
简直跟泰国那种假冒的贵价手表一样。
It's like one of those fake expensive
watches you get in Thailand.

50
00:04:12,280 --> 00:04:14,399
只有真正的专家才分得清。
Only a real expert
can tell the difference.

51
00:04:14,399 --> 00:04:19,400
我可是劳斯莱斯专家，结果被它骗得团团转。
I am a Rolls-Royce expert,
and I was completely taken in.

52
00:04:19,400 --> 00:04:24,200
其实我不是这个意思。我想说的是，这简直是赤裸裸的抄袭，
Actually, I didn't mean that.
What I meant to say was,
it's an utterly shameless rip-off,

53
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:26,800
我真不敢相信他们还能这么逍遥法外。
and I can't believe
they're getting away with it.

54
00:04:26,800 --> 00:04:31,160
那3.5升V6的性能到底怎样？
So, what about the
performance from the 3.5 litre V6?

55
00:04:31,160 --> 00:04:34,160
这真的是原装货吗？
Is that the genuine article?

56
00:04:34,160 --> 00:04:37,520
劳斯莱斯得能从静止嗖地一下冲出去。
A Rolls-Royce must be able to
whoosh away from a stand still.

57
00:04:37,520 --> 00:04:42,440
它可以很快，但绝不能让人觉得急迫，必须温柔地加速，
It can go quite quickly,
but it must never feel urgent,
it must swell very gently,

58
00:04:42,440 --> 00:04:45,239
要像交响乐般绵延。
it must be an orchestral performance.

59
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:49,440
但这车根本不是。抱歉。
Which that isn't. Sorry.

60
00:04:50,519 --> 00:04:52,799
接下来，操控感。
Next, handling.

61
00:04:52,799 --> 00:04:58,640
劳斯莱斯绝不能让司机在拐弯时太激进，那太不礼貌了。
A Rolls-Royce should never allow
its driver to corner too vigorously
because that would be bad form.

62
00:04:58,640 --> 00:05:01,199
它得让你不自觉地收回油门。
It must encourage you
to rein things back.

63
00:05:03,359 --> 00:05:08,360
显然，这点上它做得不对。非常抱歉。非常抱歉。
Clearly, it's not quite right in
that respect. Very sorry. Very sorry.

64
00:05:09,840 --> 00:05:13,520
我继续把我的贵宾们送过去。
I cracked on with the job
of delivering my VIPs.

65
00:05:13,520 --> 00:05:14,519
满意？
Happy?

66
00:05:18,220 --> 00:05:21,140
已经非常接近目的地了。
Very close to the destination.

67
00:05:24,619 --> 00:05:27,899
他们在说日语
THEY SPEAK IN JAPANESE

68
00:05:27,899 --> 00:05:30,940
什么？就这么点儿？
What? Is that it?

69
00:05:30,940 --> 00:05:32,620
哦。
Oh.

70
00:05:35,500 --> 00:05:37,859
扩音器里的人在说日语
MAN ON PA SPEAKS IN JAPANESE

71
00:05:46,979 --> 00:05:49,140
我想他们彻底被蒙住了。
I think they were completely fooled.

72
00:05:54,780 --> 00:05:58,499
正如上周有些人已经发现的，我手里有一台老旧的劳斯莱斯，
As some of you may have found out
last week, I have got an old Rolls,

73
00:05:58,499 --> 00:06:02,179
让我告诉你，Galue根本不在同一个星球上。
and let me tell you, the Galue
isn't even on the same planet.

74
00:06:02,179 --> 00:06:06,219
不过你们知道吗，这车真的让我笑了。
But you know what,
this car does make me smile.

75
00:06:07,260 --> 00:06:11,020
它一点也不装逼。
It's not taking itself too seriously.

76
00:06:11,020 --> 00:06:15,820
就是玩玩而已，有点像那些致敬乐队。
It's just a bit of fun. It's a bit
like one of those tribute bands.

77
00:06:15,820 --> 00:06:20,179
Bjorn Again, Let's Zep, the Strolling Bones.
Bjorn Again,
Let's Zep, the Strolling Bones.

78
00:06:20,179 --> 00:06:24,499
跟那些乐队一样，它知道自己不是正品，
Like those bands,
it knows it's not the real thing,

79
00:06:24,499 --> 00:06:29,620
更重要的是，它知道你也知道它不是真正的。
but, more importantly, it knows
you know it's not the real thing.

80
00:06:29,620 --> 00:06:33,619
即使到了晚上，你依旧醉得不轻。
evening you're still just as drunk,

81
00:06:33,619 --> 00:06:36,499
而且你们玩得还是挺爽的，但只花了五英镑。
and you've still had a great time,
but it only cost you a fiver.

82
00:06:46,080 --> 00:06:49,719
这车会在英国卖吗？
Is that car going to be sold
in the UK?

83
00:06:49,719 --> 00:06:51,999
不会。很好。理查德？
No. Good. Richard?

84
00:06:51,999 --> 00:06:57,679
是的。KTM 是奥地利的摩托车制造商，他们出品像 Duke 这样的车，真是棒极了。
Yes. KTM are an Austrian bike
manufacturer, and they make things
like this, the Duke, and it's great.

85
00:06:57,679 --> 00:07:00,559
但现在他们决定跨界造车，这就是成果。
But now they've decided to have
a go at a car, and here it is.

86
00:07:00,559 --> 00:07:02,520
它叫 Crossbow（十字弓）。
It's called the Crossbow.

87
00:07:02,520 --> 00:07:06,519
车身采用塑料面板，和摩托车上一样。
The body's made of plastic panels,
just like it is on the bike.

88
00:07:06,519 --> 00:07:09,039
你可以直接看到内部结构，就像摩托车那样。
You can see the innards,
like you can on the bike.

89
00:07:09,039 --> 00:07:12,400
而且开它必须戴防撞头盔，和骑摩托一样。
And you have to wear a
crash helmet to drive it,
like you do on the bike.

90
00:07:12,400 --> 00:07:14,520
它真的是一辆裸车赛道车。
It really is a stripped
out track car.

91
00:07:14,520 --> 00:07:16,720
你只能得到一个座位，一个方向盘
All you get is a seat,
a steering wheel

92
00:07:16,720 --> 00:07:21,960
再加一台2升涡轮增压的奥迪发动机，四秒就能冲到每小时60英里。
and a two-litre turbo-charged Audi
engine that's enough to take it to
60 miles an hour in four seconds.

93
00:07:21,960 --> 00:07:24,800
据说，KTM 说这车相当难驾驭，
Apparently, KTM say it is
quite a handful,

94
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:28,759
所以他们不卖给24岁以下的司机。
and as a result they won't sell it
to drivers under 24 years old.

95
00:07:28,759 --> 00:07:31,320
唯一的问题——刘易斯·汉密尔顿。
Just one thing - Lewis Hamilton.

96
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:33,159
他才23岁！
He's 23!

97
00:07:34,520 --> 00:07:41,599
关键是它要价43,000英镑，给一辆带两只额外轮子的摩托车，这价钱可真高。
The thing about that is it costs
£43,000, which seems like a lot for
a motorcycle with two extra wheels.

98
00:07:41,599 --> 00:07:45,760
不不不，算不是吧。好吧，算是的。你可以把它开过去——叫什么来着？
No, it isn't. Well, it is.
You could drive that thing
through - what's it's called?

99
00:07:45,760 --> 00:07:51,399
Oxbow？——你开着它穿过小雨，竟然还能活着到另一边。
Oxbow? - you could drive that through
a light shower and you could
come out on the other side

100
00:07:51,399 --> 00:07:54,919
而且内部器官还能不被移植到别人身上。
without your internal organs being
transplanted into someone else.

101
00:07:54,919 --> 00:08:01,720
你们两个根本不配骑摩托。活得都怕穿着皮衣进不了天堂，
You don't get bikes. You two live
in fear that you'll go through the
pearly gates with your leathers on,

102
00:08:01,720 --> 00:08:07,239
明明我已经回到地球，变成了个开车的，
knowing full well that
I'm back on Earth, as a car driver,

103
00:08:07,239 --> 00:08:09,080
顺便带走了你们的肝脏。
with your liver.

104
00:08:09,080 --> 00:08:14,480
别指望我会有什么用处，我只会把它做成帽子戴。
And don't think I'm going to do
anything useful with it because I'm
just going to make it into a hat.

105
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:17,119
我实际上随身带着一张卡，上面写着，
I actually carry a card that says,

106
00:08:17,119 --> 00:08:22,880
“我不愿在我去世后帮助杰里米·克拉克森变得有趣。”
"I do not wish to help Jeremy
Clarkson be amusing in
the event of my death."

107
00:08:22,880 --> 00:08:29,920
好吧。每年童子军都会颁发一系列他们自认重要的奖项。
Fair enough. Every year, the
Scouts make a series of awards,
which are relevant to them.

108
00:08:29,920 --> 00:08:32,639
我这儿有名单。他们刚宣布了今年的获奖者。
I've got the list here. They've
just announced this year's winners.

109
00:08:32,639 --> 00:08:37,159
往届获奖者包括查理·布尔曼和伊万·麦格雷戈，他们拿过最佳导航奖。
Previous winners have included
Charlie Boorman and Ewan MacGregor.
They won best navigation award.

110
00:08:37,159 --> 00:08:39,239
杰米·奥利弗获得了健康饮食奖。
Jamie Oliver
won the healthy eating award.

111
00:08:39,239 --> 00:08:45,400
是啊。不过雷·米尔斯可没拿过‘成年男人穿短裤服务奖’。
Yeah. Now, Ray Mears has not won
the award for services of wearing
shorts when you're a grown man.

112
00:08:45,400 --> 00:08:52,039
不过，今年他们的‘教学服务奖’
However, their award, this year,
for services to instruction

113
00:08:52,039 --> 00:08:54,440
居然颁给了……斯提格。
has gone...to the Stig.

114
00:09:00,560 --> 00:09:07,679
不过，出了个大问题。他们之前下来给他发徽章，
However, there's a problem,
a really big problem. They came
down earlier to give him his badge,

115
00:09:07,679 --> 00:09:10,279
结果他把他们给撅了。
and he attacked them.

116
00:09:10,279 --> 00:09:13,400
我们这里有实拍，真的。
We've got some footage
of it here, seriously.

117
00:09:13,400 --> 00:09:15,640
看。
Look.

118
00:09:15,640 --> 00:09:19,360
他想踩扁自己的徽章，简直恨死它了。
He's trying to stamp on
his badge, he hates it.

119
00:09:19,360 --> 00:09:23,560
于是把他给制服了。真的把斯提格揍倒在地，两个童子军一起上场。
And they took him down. They actually
took the Stig down, two Scouts.

120
00:09:25,600 --> 00:09:33,439
这真是尴尬——原来他怕童子军。
It's awkward, that. It turns
out he's terrified of Scouts.

121
00:09:33,439 --> 00:09:39,479
现在来点坏消息——这周詹姆斯溜进我常去的酒吧找我，
Now, bad news - this week, James
popped to see me at my local pub,

122
00:09:39,479 --> 00:09:45,040
把他的摩托车停在外面，并没有违规……
parked his motorcycle, outside,
not illegally...

123
00:09:45,040 --> 00:09:50,919
不，算是很体贴的说法。对，它确实违规停了，但不自私。没错。
No, very considerately. That's
right, it was illegally parked,
but not inconsiderate. Exactly.

124
00:09:50,919 --> 00:09:54,880
被罚了120英镑，120块钱。
Fined £120. 120 quid.

125
00:09:54,880 --> 00:10:00,959
好吧，听我说——我们两个最近都被偷过电视机。
Now, here's the thing, all right -
both of us, in the not too distant
past, have had televisions stolen.

126
00:10:00,959 --> 00:10:06,079
所以警察怎么能找到你那稍微违规停放的摩托车，
So how come they've got the
man power to find your slightly
illegally parked motorcycle

127
00:10:06,079 --> 00:10:08,480
却说找不到我们的电视？
when they say that can't find
our televisions?

128
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:12,999
我真是搞不懂。我打电话给停车罚单咨询热线的女士，
I don't understand it.
I rang up the woman on the parking
ticket hotline enquiry hotline

129
00:10:12,999 --> 00:10:17,880
跟她说：“你找到我的电视了吗？”她完全不知道我在说什么。
and I said to her, "Have you
found my television?" She had no
idea what I was talking about.

130
00:10:17,880 --> 00:10:22,439
我觉得如果你人生里被偷过东西……
I think that if you've had
something stolen in your life...

131
00:10:22,439 --> 00:10:25,040
这里有多少人被偷过东西？割草机……
How many people here have had
something stolen? The lawnmower...

132
00:10:25,040 --> 00:10:26,879
几乎全员。
Nearly everybody.

133
00:10:26,879 --> 00:10:30,959
警方居然可以因小小的交通违规给你开罚单，
..it should be illegal
for the police to do you
for a trivial motoring offence

134
00:10:30,959 --> 00:10:34,079
却不归还你被偷走的东西！对啊！
until they've returned whatever
it is you've had stolen! Yes!

135
00:10:34,079 --> 00:10:36,039
有人觉得……？
Does anybody here think...?

136
00:10:36,039 --> 00:10:37,799
（掌声）
APPLAUSE

137
00:10:39,719 --> 00:10:41,799
说真的……
Seriously...

138
00:10:41,799 --> 00:10:47,399
如果你在看这段，布朗先生，那就是全体英国人 100% 同意我的观点。
if you're watching this, Mr Brown,
that's 100% of British people
agree with me.

139
00:10:47,399 --> 00:10:52,679
说到 TVR……你知道它几年前被一个俄罗斯小布尔什维克买下吧？
Now, hey, TVR... You know it was
bought by a Russian
business boy, a few years ago?

140
00:10:52,679 --> 00:10:55,439
其实是他爸当成玩具套装买给他的，
Actually it was bought by his father
as a sort of play set for him,

141
00:10:55,439 --> 00:10:59,079
结果他把车冲进山坡，TVR 从此消失。真是可怜。
and he crashed it into a hillside
and now TVR's gone. Very sad.

142
00:10:59,079 --> 00:11:03,280
不过，原来他仍然拥有知识产权，
However, turns out he still owns
the intellectual property rights,

143
00:11:03,280 --> 00:11:06,760
还有模具，他说要把 TVR 复活。
and he still owns the moulds, and he
says he's going to bring TVR back.

144
00:11:06,760 --> 00:11:12,040
我们还有他和朋友们试驾新车型的照片。
We've actually got a picture
of him, testing these
new models with his friends.

145
00:11:12,040 --> 00:11:15,760
他说要先公布哪款车型先复活，
He said he was going to announce
which model would come back first,

146
00:11:15,760 --> 00:11:19,519
结果他妈叫他回屋喝茶。
but then his mum said he
had to come inside for his tea.

147
00:11:19,519 --> 00:11:21,680
喂。好消息。什么？
Hey. Great news. What?

148
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:25,519
我刚收到更多关于 Dacia Sandero 的资料。
I've been sent more
information on the Dacia Sandero.

149
00:11:25,519 --> 00:11:27,280
太棒了！
Excellent!

150
00:11:27,280 --> 00:11:30,440
太棒了。说到全新的雪铁龙 Berlingo，
Excellent. Now,
you know the new Citroen Berlingo?

151
00:11:30,440 --> 00:11:32,279
这车我们可是相当喜欢。
This is a car we like very much.

152
00:11:32,279 --> 00:11:37,640
售价不到 11,000 英镑，却是大空间车，
It costs less than £11,000, and for
that you get a big, spacious car,

153
00:11:37,640 --> 00:11:40,880
乘坐感受堪比劳斯莱斯以下的任何车型。
with the best ride of any car
under a Rolls-Royce.

154
00:11:40,880 --> 00:11:45,239
我一直想，这种车怎么能只花不到 1.1 万就做好？
I've been thinking, how do they do a
car like that for less than 11 grand?

155
00:11:45,239 --> 00:11:47,440
于是上网一搜，找到了这个。
So I went on the internet
and I found this.

156
00:11:58,079 --> 00:12:00,239
嗯。
Yep.

157
00:12:01,840 --> 00:12:06,079
之后，我找到了——就是雪铁龙的官网。
Afterwards, OK, I found this -
it's the Citroen website.

158
00:12:06,079 --> 00:12:09,239
你知道他们会把车标配的东西列出来吧？
You know how they list what
a car comes with as standard?

159
00:12:09,239 --> 00:12:15,239
当车厂开始标榜“层压前挡风玻璃”时，就能看出他们有多想撑。
You can tell when a car firm
is desperate when they've got
"laminated front wind screen".

160
00:12:15,239 --> 00:12:18,520
哇！那和什么相比？从温室偷来的玻璃片？
Wow! As opposed to what? A sheet
of glass nicked from a greenhouse?

161
00:12:18,520 --> 00:12:22,520
更好玩了，前排只有一个乘客座位。
It gets better. It's got a
"single front passenger seat".

162
00:12:22,520 --> 00:12:26,800
啊？还有手动调节的车门后视镜。
Huh? And "manually adjustable
door mirrors".

163
00:12:26,800 --> 00:12:31,480
那跟什么相比？唯一的选择不就是电动的了吗？
As opposed to what? The only
alternative is electrical, isn't it?

164
00:12:31,480 --> 00:12:36,839
这句话的意思就是它没有这个。没有电动后视镜，也没有铝合金轮毂……
That's just saying it's something it
hasn't got. It hasn't got electrical
door mirrors, no alloy wheels...

165
00:12:36,839 --> 00:12:42,520
这车挺好的，只要你想要的装备跟罗马尼亚监狱一样的。
It's a very good car, so long
as you want something that's
equipped like a Romanian jail.

166
00:12:42,520 --> 00:12:47,879
我有个问题。什么？要是这车真的不错呢？呃，那是不可能的。
I've got a question. What?
What if this turns out to be
really good? Well, it won't.

167
00:12:47,879 --> 00:12:51,040
不，就算真不错呢？不可能的，才对吧？
No, but what if it does?
Well, it won't, will it?

168
00:12:51,040 --> 00:12:55,079
这可是全新的雪佛兰科迈罗。他们真的下了功夫，外观帅炸天。
It's the new Chevy Camaro.
And they're really thought about it.
It looks brilliant.

169
00:12:55,079 --> 00:12:59,240
配备6.2升V8，引擎四周全独立悬挂。
It's got a 6.2 litre V8,
and they've given it
independent suspension all round.

170
00:12:59,240 --> 00:13:01,279
哇——！
Wooooow!

171
00:13:01,279 --> 00:13:07,640
独立？！他们看看车，就想“这车有四个独立的轮子”。
Independent?! So they've looked at
a car and thought, "It's got
four separate wheels.

172
00:13:07,640 --> 00:13:13,600
“要是把它们都当成单独的来算呢？”这不就是欧洲百年来的老把戏吗？
"What if we treated them all
sort of separate?" Like they've
been doing in Europe for 100 years?

173
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:17,240
我仍然在想，要是居然好呢？谁知道啊！
I still think what if that turns
out to be good?! We don't know yet!

174
00:13:17,240 --> 00:13:22,599
理查德，美国人擅长赶野牛。完。
Richard, the Americans are
good at herding bison. The end.

175
00:13:22,599 --> 00:13:27,599
我还是坚持它可能会好，届时大家都会想要一台。下面那玩意儿是啥？
I still maintain it might turn
out to be good, then we'll all
want one. What is this underneath?

176
00:13:27,599 --> 00:13:30,160
这是一辆沃克斯豪尔VXR，
It's a Vauxhall VXR,

177
00:13:30,160 --> 00:13:34,399
所以美国人就想，“我们得搞点精致感——”
so what the Americans have done
is they've gone, "We need
some sophistication here -

178
00:13:34,399 --> 00:13:36,640
“找澳大利亚人来搞。”
"we'll call the Australians."

179
00:13:36,640 --> 00:13:42,640
这就像说，“我想要婚礼有点格调，咱们买七箱啤酒吧。”
That is like saying, "I want
some style for my wedding,
I'll get seven crates of lager."

180
00:13:42,640 --> 00:13:46,279
你是那种，我可以给你看看帕丽斯·希尔顿的照片的人
You're the sort of person I could
show you a picture of Paris Hilton

181
00:13:46,279 --> 00:13:49,559
然后你会说，“要是她居然聪明呢？”
and you'd say, "What if she
turns out to be intelligent?"

182
00:13:49,559 --> 00:13:52,400
但要是她真的聪明呢？！真的聪明呢？！
But what if she did?!
What if she did?!

183
00:13:52,400 --> 00:13:54,479
这新闻够多了。
That's enough news.

184
00:13:54,479 --> 00:13:56,440
好，马自达。
Now, Mazda.

185
00:13:56,440 --> 00:14:01,280
多年下来，他们因生产极其实用的小车，名声响当当
Over the years, they've built up
a fearsome reputation for making
very sensible small cars

186
00:14:01,280 --> 00:14:05,560
以及史上最烂的电视广告。
and the worst television
commercials in all of human history.

187
00:14:05,560 --> 00:14:08,160
不过，这才是他们的最新力作。
This, however,
is their latest creation.

188
00:14:08,160 --> 00:14:14,120
显然，他们想给它起个能让人联想到侵略和愤怒的名字，
Plainly, they wanted to give
it a name which conjured up
an image of aggression and anger,

189
00:14:14,120 --> 00:14:17,399
但起名的活儿交给了伯明翰的某个人，
but the job of naming it was given
to somebody from Birmingham,

190
00:14:17,399 --> 00:14:21,040
于是就叫“Furai”了。
so it's ended up being called
the Furai.

191
00:14:21,040 --> 00:14:27,879
底盘源自美国勒芒赛车，和欧洲的同款一样，只是胖了点。
The chassis is from an American Le
Mans racer, which is the same as a
European Le Mans racer, only fatter.

192
00:14:27,879 --> 00:14:33,359
车身——显然是被痴迷蝙蝠侠的人设计的。
Body - that was clearly designed
by someone with a Batman fixation.

193
00:14:33,359 --> 00:14:37,959
我觉得它相当酷——不过要是你把它带去电影首映，
I think it looks brilliant - although
if you take it to a film premiere,

194
00:14:37,959 --> 00:14:41,200
它大概会去揍它的“姐妹”车型。
it'll probably take a swing
at its sister.

195
00:14:41,200 --> 00:14:43,520
当然，只是传说而已。
Allegedly, of course.

196
00:14:43,520 --> 00:14:48,400
发动机，转子式，1.9升，460马力，
The engine, Wankel,
1.9 litre, 460 brake horsepower,

197
00:14:48,400 --> 00:14:51,800
油耗2.6英里/加仑。
2.6 miles to the gallon.

198
00:14:51,800 --> 00:14:57,600
而且恼人的是坏了，导致我们不能把它开到测试跑道上。
And, annoyingly, broken.
Which means we can't put
it round our test track.

199
00:14:57,600 --> 00:15:02,639
所以，我改回回答观众来信中的问题，我这儿就有那封信。
Instead, I'm going to answer
a question that a viewer has asked.
I have their letter here.

200
00:15:02,639 --> 00:15:05,000
信里写道：“亲爱的所谓Top Gear，
It says, "Dear so called Top Gear,

201
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:10,520
“我知道有很多
又炫又有戏的超级跑车
我可以买……”
" I'm aware that there are many
elegant and dramatic supercars
that I could buy..."

202
00:15:10,520 --> 00:15:14,680
类似的东西。 “..但是，鉴于我眼睛做了个糟糕的手术，
Things like these. "..but as I'm the
victim of a botched eye operation,

203
00:15:14,680 --> 00:15:18,479
“我想要的，是一辆
灾难级丑陋的超级跑车。”
"what I want is a supercar
that is catastrophically ugly.

204
00:15:18,479 --> 00:15:21,959
“能帮忙吗？” 是啊，我想我能。
"Can you help?" Yes, I think I can.

205
00:15:23,999 --> 00:15:26,399
这可能就是
你们的救星。
This could be the
answer to your problems.

206
00:15:26,399 --> 00:15:32,600
这是一款德国新出的超级跑车——说实话，长得一点也不咋地。
It's a new supercar from Germany -
and, well, it's not exactly a looker.

207
00:15:34,199 --> 00:15:36,039
我这么说吧。
Let me put it this way.

208
00:15:36,039 --> 00:15:37,720
当杰里米开阿尔法8C的时候…
When Jeremy did the Alfa 8C...

209
00:15:40,040 --> 00:15:44,920
…摄像组发现，找不到一个不把车子拍得帅呆的角度。
..the camera crew found there
wasn't a single angle that didn't
make the car look brilliant.

210
00:15:44,920 --> 00:15:47,960
这车恰恰相反。
This is the exact opposite.

211
00:15:47,960 --> 00:15:50,800
不行。 不行。
No. No.

212
00:15:50,800 --> 00:15:52,640
真的不行。
Really, no.

213
00:15:55,400 --> 00:15:58,799
还有个致命问题——名字。
And then there's the problem
of the name.

214
00:15:58,799 --> 00:16:06,279
有没有那种性感的名字，像其他所有帅车都有的——Vanquish、Viper、Raptor之类？
Does it have one of those sexy ones,
like all the sexiest cars have -
Vanquish, Viper, Raptor?

215
00:16:06,279 --> 00:16:10,040
没有，叫Gumpert。
No. It's called a Gumpert.

216
00:16:10,040 --> 00:16:15,440
那外形只能让妈妈爱不释手，名字却像北方喜剧演员的冷笑话。
So, it's got looks
only a mother could love and a
name like a Northern comedian.

217
00:16:17,440 --> 00:16:22,000
想开这玩意儿，你得掏掉二十五万英镑。
And for the privilege of driving it,
you'll need £250,000.

218
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:26,000
那么问题来了，花这钱到底能买到啥？
This does beg the question,
what do you get for your money?

219
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:30,200
当然，你别指望买到一套惊艳的、类似Zonda的内饰。
Certainly, you're not buying a
wondrous Zonda-esque interior.

220
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:38,360
这车里全是从奥迪那里随便拼凑来的碎件。
It's just a random collection of
bits from Audi.

221
00:16:40,199 --> 00:16:45,440
嗯，是啊，不过别指望有夜视或厕所。
Well, yes, but don't go looking
for night-vision or a bathroom.

222
00:16:45,440 --> 00:16:50,159
还有这后视摄像头，也算不上。
And this, the rear-view camera,
doesn't count.

223
00:16:50,159 --> 00:16:52,600
那是必备的，因为根本没有后窗。
That's a necessity.
There's no back window.

224
00:16:54,759 --> 00:16:59,759
Gumpert的选配就只有这种——牵引力控制。
Options on the Gumpert are things
like this - the traction control.

225
00:17:01,360 --> 00:17:06,999
现在很多车都有牵引力控制，但Gumpert的这玩意儿真是奇葩。
Now, lots of cars have traction
control, but the Gumpert's
is really quite anorakey.

226
00:17:06,999 --> 00:17:12,159
它不是按钮，而是旋钮，你可以精细调节。所以，接下来是Hammerhead。
It's not a button, it's a knob.
You can adjust it so you can be
precise. So, Hammerhead coming up.

227
00:17:12,159 --> 00:17:13,719
我熟悉这个弯。
I know this corner.

228
00:17:13,719 --> 00:17:16,160
大概是17%吧。
17%, I think.

229
00:17:22,960 --> 00:17:25,120
嗯，那…
Yeah, that...

230
00:17:25,120 --> 00:17:27,680
别担心。
But worry not.

231
00:17:27,680 --> 00:17:31,360
要是这招不行，还有一大堆别的调节项。
If that doesn't work out,
there are whole load of
other things you can adjust.

232
00:17:31,360 --> 00:17:36,000
你可以调前倾角、离地高度、弹簧硬度，
You can change the camber,
the ride height, the spring tension,

233
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:38,759
减震阻尼、压缩回弹以及防倾杆。
the damper, bump and rebound
and the anti-roll bar.

234
00:17:40,439 --> 00:17:42,520
哦耶！
Oh, yeah!

235
00:17:42,520 --> 00:17:47,800
看哪，蒙特卡洛、克劳迪娅·希弗，坐着你们的超级跑车——“能不能现在直接去派对啊？”
There you are, Monte Carlo, Claudia
Schiffer, in your supercar -
"Please can we go to the party now?"

236
00:17:47,800 --> 00:17:52,320
“不，等等。还有一堆弯，我要再调一点前倾角。”
"No, hold on. A lot of corners. I'm
gonna dial in some extra camber."

237
00:17:54,599 --> 00:17:56,999
调好前倾角后，我开始…
With the camber adjusted,
I went for...

238
00:17:56,999 --> 00:17:58,439
哎呀，真是…
Oh, bugger.

239
00:18:01,239 --> 00:18:05,720
我觉得这些设定根本玩不了，还是别动它们了！
I think some of those settings are
not an option. Just leave them alone!

240
00:18:08,039 --> 00:18:13,199
我在自行车上也遇到过同样的事，结果只会把局面搞得更烂。
I've had this experience with
one of my bikes. All you ever do is
make things worse.

241
00:18:14,240 --> 00:18:19,919
这车唯一缺的一个选项，我倒是挺喜欢的。
There is one option this car doesn't
have, and it's one I quite like.

242
00:18:19,919 --> 00:18:22,840
那就是座椅前后移动的功能。
The option to move your seat
backwards and forwards.

243
00:18:22,840 --> 00:18:28,439
因为古姆佩特的人受够了司机们随意调座位，
That's because the Gumpert people
got fed up with drivers
moving their seats around

244
00:18:28,439 --> 00:18:31,079
把他们完美的重量分配搞得乱七八糟。
and messing up their perfect
weight distribution.

245
00:18:34,119 --> 00:18:40,160
所以，丑得要命的外观、坐不动的座椅，还有只有刘易斯·汉密尔顿才能看懂的玩意儿。
So, minging looks, seats you
can't move and gizmos only Lewis
Hamilton can make sense of.

246
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:44,999
现在你应该明白了，这可不是海岸巡航车。
I think you're getting the picture by
now that this is no Riviera cruiser.

247
00:18:44,999 --> 00:18:51,520
他们最快的版本 Apollo Race，马力高达800匹，但如果你已经拿到了驾照，
Their fastest version, the Apollo
Race, has 800 brake horsepower, but
if you've passed your driving test,

248
00:18:51,520 --> 00:18:58,360
他们还有所谓的入门版，650马力。这个是中等配置。
they do do what they call
an entry-level version, 650 brake
horsepower. This is the mid-range.

249
00:18:58,360 --> 00:19:03,479
我想他们会叫它 Popular Plus——700马力。
I suppose they'd call it the
Popular Plus - 700 brake horsepower.

250
00:19:05,720 --> 00:19:08,279
从这里开始，一切都变得好玩起来
And this is where
it all starts to come good

251
00:19:08,279 --> 00:19:11,999
因为不管你选哪款古姆佩特，它都快得飞起。
because whichever Gumpert you choose,
it's going to be fast.

252
00:19:19,879 --> 00:19:21,080
我的天啊！
Ye gods!

253
00:19:24,560 --> 00:19:27,119
这简直是另一个层次！
This is just something else!

254
00:19:28,199 --> 00:19:33,559
发动机是奥迪的4.2升V8，加了双涡轮，
The engine is Audi's 4.2 litre V8,
but with added twin turbos,

255
00:19:33,559 --> 00:19:36,800
外壳全是轻质碳纤维。
all wrapped up in
featherweight carbon fibre.

256
00:19:37,840 --> 00:19:40,120
0-60秒——三秒。
0-60 - three seconds.

257
00:19:40,120 --> 00:19:43,799
最高时速——224英里每小时。
Top speed - 224mph.

258
00:19:43,799 --> 00:19:48,080
好了，看看我们这条普通跑道能跑出多少。
So, let's see how much of that
we can get on our modest runway.

259
00:19:52,479 --> 00:19:55,439
200公里每小时，也就是120英里。
That's 200 kilometres per hour.
That's 120 mph.

260
00:19:58,559 --> 00:20:01,959
280公里每小时，已经相当快了。
That's 280 kilometres an hour,
which is very fast.

261
00:20:05,279 --> 00:20:07,360
300公里每小时。
300 kilometres an hour.

262
00:20:07,360 --> 00:20:10,000
我想我要开始失控了。
I'm gonna start breaking, I think.

263
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:12,519
186英里每小时
That's 186 miles an hour

264
00:20:12,519 --> 00:20:14,879
在1.7英里内。
in 1.7 miles.

265
00:20:16,400 --> 00:20:22,679
当你进弯时，只要别动啥东西，简直太爽了。
And when you get to a corner, just
as long as you've not been fiddling
with anything, it is brilliant.

266
00:20:28,919 --> 00:20:29,999
这抓地力！
The grip!

267
00:20:29,999 --> 00:20:33,680
我的眼睛都快跑到头的另一边去了！
My eyes are a foot
that side of my head!

268
00:20:36,400 --> 00:20:41,919
突然你会明白，为什么这玩意儿看起来像狒狒屁股上的痘子。
Suddenly you realise why this thing
looks like a boil on the buttock
of a baboon.

269
00:20:41,919 --> 00:20:45,919
它有下压力，那些洞、鳍和格栅都是为此设计的。
It's got downforce, that's what all
those holes, fins and grills are for.

270
00:20:55,919 --> 00:21:02,999
如果你想在蒙特卡洛的赌场广场上炫耀停车，这车恐怕不适合你。
If you want a supercar you can park
with pride in Monte Carlo's Casino
Square, this probably isn't for you.

271
00:21:04,119 --> 00:21:08,320
还有很多别的超跑能更好地完成这件事。
There are many other cars that
will do that job much better.

272
00:21:08,320 --> 00:21:13,279
但古姆佩特的哥们儿们在他们那小小的德国工厂里走的是另一条路。
But the Gumpert guys in their
little German factory have
gone down another path.

273
00:21:13,279 --> 00:21:14,560
硬核街头。
Hardcore Street.

274
00:21:17,399 --> 00:21:23,000
我真相信，在这条赛道上，老夸西莫多（Quasimodo）能把所有超跑全部干掉。
I do believe that on this track
old Quasimodo here could destroy
every supercar alive.

275
00:21:38,320 --> 00:21:45,239
你真的在暗示这车在赛道上会比那些真快的车还快吗？
Are you really suggesting this is
gonna be quicker round the track
that lots of the really fast cars?

276
00:21:45,239 --> 00:21:48,560
它快得离谱，但我跟你说，这车最惊人之处是——
It is unbelievably quick, but I tell
you the amazing thing about this car.

277
00:21:48,560 --> 00:21:51,280
你记得我说它产生下压力把它压在地面上吧？
You know I said it generates
downforce to stick it to the road?

278
00:21:51,280 --> 00:21:58,520
古姆佩特说它的下压力大到可以倒着开，甚至还能贴在车顶上……
Well, Gumpert say it generates so
much that it could drive upside down
and still stick to the roof...

279
00:21:58,520 --> 00:22:03,079
别被这老套的说法骗了！每支F1车队都说他们的车能倒着跑。
Don't fall for that old chestnut!
Every Formula One team says you
could drive our cars upside down.

280
00:22:03,079 --> 00:22:06,880
他们之所以这么说，只是因为我们没法把他们的说法证伪。
The only reason they say that is
because we can't prove them wrong.

281
00:22:06,880 --> 00:22:08,999
是啊，但Gumpert要给我们证明一下。
Yeah, but Gumpert
are going to prove it.

282
00:22:08,999 --> 00:22:11,839
他们造了一台还能倒着跑的发动机。
They've built an engine
that will work upside down.

283
00:22:11,839 --> 00:22:14,680
还有那个隧道？他们找到了一个能在里面搞的隧道。
And the tunnel? And they found
a tunnel they can do it in.

284
00:22:14,680 --> 00:22:20,320
所以得开多快才能产生足够的下压力或上升力把它粘住？
So how fast do you have to
drive to generate enough
downforce or upforce to stick it?

285
00:22:20,320 --> 00:22:25,520
190英里每小时。所以他们要找个人以190英里每小时的速度在隧道的顶棚上行驶，
190 miles an hour. So they're gonna
get someone to drive at 190mph
down the roof of a tunnel,

286
00:22:25,520 --> 00:22:28,559
在路标、风扇和灯光之间灵活穿梭！
swerving between all the signposts,
fans and lights!

287
00:22:28,559 --> 00:22:31,679
关键是，他们已经找到了合适的隧道，
That's the thing, they found
the tunnel to do it in,

288
00:22:31,679 --> 00:22:36,039
但还没找到够蠢敢开的人。
but they've not yet found anyone
stupid enough to drive it.

289
00:22:36,039 --> 00:22:38,320
好吧，这是最后一集了。
Well, this is the last show.

290
00:22:38,320 --> 00:22:40,600
不行，我不行。
No, I can't.

291
00:22:40,600 --> 00:22:42,759
我不能，我忙。
I can't. I'm busy.

292
00:22:42,759 --> 00:22:45,599
我在给……我的马刷漆。
I'm painting...my horse.

293
00:22:45,599 --> 00:22:49,959
我做不到。不过我们现在得弄清楚它在我们赛道上跑多快，
I can't do it.
Anyway, we must now find out
how fast it goes round our track,

294
00:22:49,959 --> 00:22:53,120
也就是说得让我们这位温顺的赛车手来开。
which means we must put it in the
hands of our tame racing driver.

295
00:22:53,120 --> 00:22:59,759
有人说他连穿袜子都不可能。
Some say it's impossible
for him to wear socks.

296
00:22:59,759 --> 00:23:04,000
还能用他的睾丸打开啤酒瓶。
And he can open a beer bottle
with his testes.

297
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:07,239
我们只知道他叫斯提格。
All we know is he's called the Stig.

298
00:23:07,239 --> 00:23:09,680
他出发了，倒也没啥惊天动地的起步。
And he's off, not a scorching start.

299
00:23:09,680 --> 00:23:13,960
斯提格正小心翼翼地递出那海量动力。
Stig just carefully metering out
the power, of which there is a lot.

300
00:23:13,960 --> 00:23:19,079
现在进入第一个弯，希望他能加速，让下压力发挥作用。
First corner now, hopefully
he will be going faster
to get that downforce working.

301
00:23:19,079 --> 00:23:21,359
这可真帅，我对它寄予厚望。
That is neat,
I've got high hopes for this.

302
00:23:22,679 --> 00:23:25,479
MUSIC: "Daniel" by Elton John
MUSIC: "Daniel" by Elton John

303
00:23:27,920 --> 00:23:33,159
是啊，斯提格显然还是被艾尔顿·约翰感动着呢。
Yeah, Stig is apparently
still touched by Elton John.

304
00:23:33,159 --> 00:23:35,600
这在芝加哥的控制简直完美。
That is fantastically
controlled through Chicago.

305
00:23:35,600 --> 00:23:37,559
现在是锤头弯，慢点儿。
Hammerhead now, slower corner.

306
00:23:37,559 --> 00:23:41,080
要是那套花哨的空气动力学作不了事，就麻烦了。
Could be in trouble if the fancy
aerodynamics can't do their stuff.

307
00:23:41,080 --> 00:23:44,920
毫无戏剧性，我估计这就是这车的秘密所在。
It's so undramatic and I expect
that could be this car's secret.

308
00:23:47,440 --> 00:23:51,640
后续——真的现在把它撑开，他会不会得抬起？
The follow-through - really pin
it open now, will he have to lift?

309
00:23:51,640 --> 00:23:53,720
不大可能！
Not likely!

310
00:23:53,720 --> 00:23:58,520
简直能看到它被压进柏油路面，拐弯时平得像赛车。
You can almost see it being pressed
into the tarmac, it's so flat through
the corners like a racing car.

311
00:23:59,639 --> 00:24:02,840
终于回甩，冲过终点线。
Finally biting back,
and across the line.

312
00:24:07,480 --> 00:24:10,040
等等，等等，等等！
Hang on, hang on. Wait!

313
00:24:10,040 --> 00:24:15,640
要是你没错，它就要和Zonda、Ascari一块儿上榜了……
If you're right, it's gonna be up
with the Zonda, the Ascari...

314
00:24:15,640 --> 00:24:18,919
没错，Ascari用了1分17秒3的成绩。
Yep, Ascari did it in 1.17.3.

315
00:24:18,919 --> 00:24:24,679
Gumbert用了1分17秒1！
The Gumbert did it in it 1.17.1!

316
00:24:24,679 --> 00:24:26,639
它是最快的！
It is the fastest!

317
00:24:31,079 --> 00:24:33,280
破我们赛道史上最快纪录。
Fastest ever around our track.

318
00:24:34,799 --> 00:24:42,160
这真是惊人，因为这是哈蒙德今年第一次在我们赛道上开车。
That really is incredible because
that is the first car Hammond has
driven round our circuit this year.

319
00:24:42,160 --> 00:24:46,840
它已经冲到排行榜首位……哈蒙德根本赶不上。
And it's gone to the top of the
leaderboard...which he can't reach.

320
00:24:48,999 --> 00:24:52,040
我能，我能！我只需要先热身一下。
I can, I can! I just need a run up.

321
00:24:52,040 --> 00:24:53,999
这可不怎么体面啊。
This is going to be undignified.

322
00:24:55,600 --> 00:24:58,280
这玩意儿没成功。
It's not worked.

323
00:24:58,280 --> 00:25:04,760
开动啦！
It's on!

324
00:25:06,040 --> 00:25:08,240
好，这已经算一次……
OK, that's one...

325
00:25:08,240 --> 00:25:12,440
这已经砸碎了一条单圈纪录，真是字面意思。
that's one lap record smashed,
quite literally.

326
00:25:12,440 --> 00:25:15,160
接下来，看看能不能再来一次。
Now, let's see if we can't
deal with another one.

327
00:25:15,160 --> 00:25:19,319
下面是一份开过我们这辆价格亲民的车的明星名单。
This is a list of the stars who've
driven our reasonably priced car

328
00:25:19,319 --> 00:25:26,360
而西蒙·考威尔已经在过去两季坐上了冠军宝座，我们觉得已经够久了。
and Simon Cowell has now been at
the top for the last two series,
which we think is long enough.

329
00:25:26,360 --> 00:25:32,120
于是我们回去翻看了所有开过我们旧款性价比车的嘉宾，
So what we've done is we went back
and looked at all the people who
drove our old reasonably priced car,

330
00:25:32,120 --> 00:25:36,400
找到了最大牌的车迷，再次邀请他回来。
found the biggest petrol head
and invited him back.

331
00:25:36,400 --> 00:25:38,800
各位观众，请欢迎杰·凯！
Ladies and gentlemen,
please welcome Jay Kay!

332
00:25:44,399 --> 00:25:46,759
怎么样？请坐。
How are you? Have a seat.

333
00:25:46,759 --> 00:25:48,519
谢谢。
Thank you.

334
00:25:48,519 --> 00:25:49,880
哇——！
Wa-hay!

335
00:25:50,960 --> 00:25:52,720
哇——！
Wa-hay!

336
00:25:52,720 --> 00:25:58,280
你一直在纠缠想来这儿。说真的，已经有好几周没……
You have been nagging to be here.
Honestly, there hasn't
been a week go by...

337
00:25:58,280 --> 00:26:00,440
你上次来这里多久了？
How long is it since you were here?

338
00:26:00,440 --> 00:26:05,279
我在第一季就在这，我想我是第二个上来的。
I was here on the first series,
I think I was the second guy.

339
00:26:05,279 --> 00:26:11,839
你是第二位嘉宾，之后根本没间隔一周。
You were the second guest ever.
There hasn't been a week
really gone by since then

340
00:26:11,839 --> 00:26:15,040
当你不在电话里说“我能回来吗”时
when you haven't been on the
phone going can I come back?

341
00:26:15,040 --> 00:26:21,599
我得说，我感觉被排除在外，孤单，坐在厨房里看着它想，
I have to say I felt left out,
lonely, sat in my kitchen
watching it thinking,

342
00:26:21,599 --> 00:26:23,320
“我什么时候回来？”
"When will I come back?

343
00:26:23,320 --> 00:26:28,520
“我什么时候能打败那个穿护裆的家伙？” 哦，西蒙？
"When will I beat the man
with the codpiece?" Oh, Simon?

344
00:26:28,520 --> 00:26:30,320
护裆考威尔！
Codpiece Cowell!

345
00:26:30,320 --> 00:26:34,399
我刚想起来点事儿，你跟研究员说了什么来着？
I've just remembered something, what
was it you said to the researcher?

346
00:26:34,399 --> 00:26:38,399
我们打电话说能不能回来……我说我在这儿打仗。
When we rang up and
said can you come back...
I said I'm down here for war.

347
00:26:38,399 --> 00:26:41,080
他来了！我在这儿打仗！
He did! I'm down here for war!

348
00:26:41,080 --> 00:26:48,400
我不是来胡闹的，也不是来抢第13名的，也不是来打败James Blunt的，我是来争第一的。
I'm not here to muck about, not here
to be 13th, not here to beat James
Blunt, I'm here to be on the top.

349
00:26:48,400 --> 00:26:51,079
所以第一名，别的都不行？
So first or nothing else will do?

350
00:26:51,079 --> 00:26:54,520
我也不是来超越James Blunt的专辑销量的。
I'm not here to beat James
Blunt's album sales either.

351
00:26:54,520 --> 00:26:57,919
你总共卖了多少？大概2500万吧。
How many have you sold in total?
25 million or something.

352
00:26:57,919 --> 00:27:01,919
2500万，而你甚至不会读谱。谢谢大家。
25 million and you can't read music.
Thank you, everybody.

353
00:27:01,919 --> 00:27:05,599
谢谢。掌声
Thank you.
APPLAUSE

354
00:27:07,199 --> 00:27:09,799
那可真是专辑不少啊。
That is a lot of albums.

355
00:27:09,799 --> 00:27:13,679
我不会费劲去列出你所有的东西
I won't bother going through
the list of everything you've got

356
00:27:13,679 --> 00:27:16,359
因为节目只有一个小时。
because the programme
is only an hour long.

357
00:27:16,359 --> 00:27:18,719
不过你现在到底有几辆车？
But how many cars
have you got these days?

358
00:27:18,719 --> 00:27:22,759
一共有37辆车，包括摩托车，
There are 37 vehicles,
that's including motorbikes,

359
00:27:22,759 --> 00:27:24,839
还有工作人员用车。
and staff cars.

360
00:27:24,839 --> 00:27:27,719
工作人员用车！
Staff cars!

361
00:27:27,719 --> 00:27:32,840
他们车上可没有挂小旗子和纳粹标志！
They don't have little flags
and swastikas on!

362
00:27:32,840 --> 00:27:36,640
前面也不是两轮，后面也不是半履带。
Or two wheels at the front
and a half track at the back.

363
00:27:36,640 --> 00:27:41,519
自从你上次来后，有哪些主要变化？
Since you were last here,
what have been the main changes?

364
00:27:41,519 --> 00:27:46,199
主要是我莫名其妙迷上了保时捷。
The main stuff is that I've got into
Porsches, for some unknown reason.

365
00:27:46,199 --> 00:27:53,759
大约三四年前，我买了台 RS Touring，配有原厂天窗，后排 911，
About three or four years ago,
I bought an RS Touring, which is
the factory sunroof, rear-seat 911,

366
00:27:53,759 --> 00:27:57,439
侧面是 Carrera，车拱宽大，2.7 发动机。
Carrera down the side,
wide arches, 2.7 engine.

367
00:27:57,439 --> 00:28:04,199
随后我入手了 911 3T GRS，因为我觉得这车会成为未来的经典……
Then I got a 911 3T GRS, the reason
being because I thought this car
is gonna be a future classic...

368
00:28:04,199 --> 00:28:07,840
997 版？997 GT 3RS，没错。
Present at 997? A 997 GT 3RS, yeah.

369
00:28:07,840 --> 00:28:13,639
后来我又搞到一台轻量化的 911 RS。
I've then subsequently gone and
got myself a 911 RS light weight.

370
00:28:13,639 --> 00:28:19,239
我真的仍然看不出 911 的魅力。对吧。
I still genuinely don't get
the appeal of 911s. Right.

371
00:28:19,239 --> 00:28:22,199
你开过现代的 Turbo 吗？
Have you driven a modern-day Turbo?

372
00:28:22,199 --> 00:28:24,960
有段时间没开了。
Not for a while.

373
00:28:24,960 --> 00:28:27,800
甚至是 GT3 RS 也没开过。
Or even a GT3 RS.

374
00:28:27,800 --> 00:28:31,039
我开着它想着，‘其实这车还挺不错的’，
I drive that and think,
"Actually, this is a nice car,"

375
00:28:31,039 --> 00:28:36,760
结果前几天我玩起了新 GT2，那款 Turbo。
then I got into a GT2 the other day,
the new GT2. The Turbo, yeah.

376
00:28:36,760 --> 00:28:40,480
简直是恶心到极点，丑爆了。
It's absolutely, hideously horrid.

377
00:28:40,480 --> 00:28:44,600
到底哪儿不好？它把 911 应有的都给实现了。
What don't you like about it? It does
everything you expect a 911 to do.

378
00:28:44,600 --> 00:28:50,000
你明白我说的前端弹跳和推头是什么意思吗？
Do you know what I mean by
that front end bounce
and that understeer?

379
00:28:50,000 --> 00:28:55,559
一动手解决推头，它立马就变成要命的转向不足。
If you do anything about the
understeer, they switch immediately
to death-dealing oversteer.

380
00:28:55,559 --> 00:28:58,759
可能是你开法不对？
Could it be you're not
driving it properly?

381
00:28:58,759 --> 00:29:00,560
我已经打方向盘了！
I turned the steering wheel!

382
00:29:00,560 --> 00:29:08,080
你这轻量化的车……散热式的。是的，散热式的迟早会杀了你。
That light weight you've got...
Air-cooled. Yeah, the air-cooled one
is one day going to kill you.

383
00:29:08,080 --> 00:29:13,959
它现在正躲在你车库里算计怎么干掉你。现场有人有 911 吗？
It's sitting in your garage now
plotting how it's going to do it.
Has anyone here got a 911?

384
00:29:13,959 --> 00:29:16,159
看，都已经被干掉了。
See, they've all been killed.

385
00:29:16,159 --> 00:29:20,600
本来正要上路，结果全挂树上了。
They were on their way and they're
all now in a tree like that.

386
00:29:20,600 --> 00:29:23,120
我真的不懂它们。太牛了。
I just don't get them. Brilliant.

387
00:29:23,120 --> 00:29:26,999
还有好多别的事儿。是啊。
There are a number
of other things. Yeah.

388
00:29:26,999 --> 00:29:29,879
他有辆梅赛德斯·格罗塞尔。
He's got a Mercedes Grosser.

389
00:29:29,879 --> 00:29:33,799
我的那台以前是可可·香奈儿的。真的是香奈儿的？
Mine was owned by Coco Chanel. It
was actually owned by Coco Chanel?

390
00:29:33,799 --> 00:29:37,679
我的那台是埃及大使的。
Mine was owned by the
Egyptian ambassador.

391
00:29:37,679 --> 00:29:42,040
我一坐进去就全喷上 No.5。
When I get in it,
I just cover myself in No.5.

392
00:29:42,040 --> 00:29:47,600
你现在还有辆 CSL 宝马。说说 GQ 奖项吧。
And you've got a CSL BMW now.
Tell us about the GQ awards.

393
00:29:47,600 --> 00:29:51,280
是啊，我们还有共同点，都拿过奖……
Yes, another thing we've got in
common, we've both won awards...

394
00:29:51,280 --> 00:29:53,960
你拿了最差穿着奖，我拿了年度风格男。
You got Worst Dressed Man,
I got Style Man of the Year.

395
00:29:55,239 --> 00:29:57,119
不过……
Mind you...

396
00:29:57,119 --> 00:29:59,519
亲爱的，我喜欢他们。
Look, dear, I like them.

397
00:29:59,519 --> 00:30:04,040
别闹了！让后排的观众看看。根本没问题！
Get off! Show the people at the back.
There's nothing wrong with them!

398
00:30:04,040 --> 00:30:07,160
年度风格？（笑声）
Style of the year?
LAUGHTER

399
00:30:07,160 --> 00:30:09,159
他们很帅！不过我觉得一点也不帅。
They're nice! It's not nice.

400
00:30:09,159 --> 00:30:12,959
真丑。就因为 Alpinestars 不给你造鞋子。
It's hideous. Just because
Alpinestars don't make you shoes.

401
00:30:12,959 --> 00:30:16,359
不，因为我去鞋店会说，
“你们有一双鞋吗？”
No, cos I go to a shoe shop and say,
"Have you got a pair of shoes?"

402
00:30:16,359 --> 00:30:19,400
“你们有一双”
适合河马的鞋子吗？
"Have you got a pair
of shoes for a hippo?"

403
00:30:21,520 --> 00:30:27,959
我们已经聊够了车子的话题。
和你聊天真开心，我们真的
共享同样的热情。
We have talked about cars enough.
It's great talking to you. We do
genuinely share the same passions.

404
00:30:27,959 --> 00:30:30,759
我们确实喜欢同样的发动机。
We do like the same motors.

405
00:30:30,759 --> 00:30:34,439
我们真的有同类的车子。
是啊，来吧，圈速。
We do have the same sort of cars.
Yeah. Right, the lap.

406
00:30:34,439 --> 00:30:40,479
是啊，你上次来的时候，
还是老斯提格。现在的新斯提格
恢复后怎样了？
Yeah. When you came the last time,
it was old Stig. What is new
Stig like now he's regenerated?

407
00:30:40,479 --> 00:30:45,159
我和新斯提格一起出过场。他已经是大师级了，是吧？
I have been out with the new Stig.
He's in the master class, isn't he?

408
00:30:45,159 --> 00:30:49,319
我刚刚在那辆C63里跑了一圈。他是个极其出色的司机。
I've just been out in that C63.
He is an extremely good driver.

409
00:30:49,319 --> 00:30:52,799
他比刘易斯·汉密尔顿、奈杰尔·曼塞尔和马克·韦伯还快。
He is quicker than Lewis Hamilton,
Nigel Mansell and Mark Webber.

410
00:30:52,799 --> 00:30:58,520
有意思的是，
和他聊天时……
我们刚吃完晚饭，正聊得热火朝天，
The funny thing is,
when you're talking to him....
We'd just had dinner, chatting away,

411
00:30:58,520 --> 00:31:00,959
我问他想吃啥。
“你要来块排骨配凉拌卷心菜吗？”
I asked what he was going to have.
"You gonna have ribs and coleslaw?"

412
00:31:00,959 --> 00:31:04,760
你突然发现自己在和这个带屏幕的家伙聊天。
You suddenly find you are talking
to this guy with this screen.

413
00:31:04,760 --> 00:31:09,760
情况是这样的，他把它抬起来透透气，
你也跟着这么干，
What happens, he lifts it up for
a bit of air, you start doing that,

414
00:31:09,760 --> 00:31:16,359
然后他……又把它关上。
他在过滤二氧化碳，
只能靠纯氮生存。
then he goes...and shuts it again.
He is filtering out the carbon
dioxide. He runs on pure nitrogen.

415
00:31:16,359 --> 00:31:20,160
不管怎样，他给你指点了吧？是的，他确实指点了。
Anyway, he coached you? He did.

416
00:31:20,160 --> 00:31:25,280
你跑了九圈。
显然，这周没必要说，
你觉得自己进步到哪儿了？
You had your nine laps. Obviously,
there's no point saying this week,
where do you think you've come?

417
00:31:25,280 --> 00:31:28,199
你想在这儿，对吧？
You want to be here, don't you?

418
00:31:28,199 --> 00:31:32,440
还能说什么呢，当然，当然，当然！
What can I say, but yes, yes, yes!

419
00:31:32,440 --> 00:31:35,759
比下个格莱美还多？没错！
More than the next Grammy? Yes!

420
00:31:35,759 --> 00:31:41,280
我的意思是，你知道吗，
路人会拦住我问，
‘你什么时候回《Top Gear》？
I mean, do you know,
people stop me in the street and go,
"When are you back on Top Gear?

421
00:31:41,280 --> 00:31:45,320
‘你什么时候能打败西蒙·考尔？’
他们根本不在乎
哔——的音乐！
"When are you going to beat
Simon Cowell." They don't give
a BLEEP about the music!

422
00:31:48,560 --> 00:31:52,960
那就快点开始吧！不，不要。
西蒙·考尔是……哎呀！
Get on with it then! No, no.
Simon Cowell is... Agh!

423
00:31:52,960 --> 00:31:56,360
那就是西蒙·考尔现在在家里干的事！不！
That is what Simon Cowell
is doing at home now! No!

424
00:31:56,360 --> 00:32:00,080
谁想看他的圈速？
观众：要！好。
Who wants to see his lap?
AUDIENCE: Yes! OK.

425
00:32:00,080 --> 00:32:02,320
尖叫声
SCREECHING

426
00:32:02,320 --> 00:32:06,320
开局不错。这就是那一次，我得把Codpiece先生甩在身后。
Nice start. This is the one,
I must beat Mr Codpiece.

427
00:32:09,280 --> 00:32:13,439
来看看那个弯。
冲刺！
Let's have a look at that corner.
Scrubbing!

428
00:32:14,999 --> 00:32:17,399
哎呀！
Agh!

429
00:32:17,399 --> 00:32:23,920
我们为什么这么生气？
因为它是个没胆量的美国哔——，
我恨透了！
Why are we angry?
Because it is a gutless piece
of American BLEEP and I hate it!

430
00:32:23,920 --> 00:32:30,119
我们开始把一点点
戈登·拉姆齐的帕尔马干酪
从这哔——上切下来吧。
Let's start shaping tiny
bits of Gordon Ramsay parmesan
cheese off this BLEEP.

431
00:32:30,119 --> 00:32:34,640
戈登·拉姆齐……快点交卷，你这笨蛋！
Gordon Ramsay...
Go on, turn in, you pillock!

432
00:32:34,640 --> 00:32:39,399
来啊，来啊，来啊，来啊，来啊！我本来能做得更紧凑。
Come on, come on, come on,
come on, come on!
I'd have done that tighter.

433
00:32:39,399 --> 00:32:44,879
来啊！你真是个没胆量的美国哔——！说真的。
Come on! You really are a gutless
bit of Yankee BLEEP! Honestly.

434
00:32:46,199 --> 00:32:50,080
你在切入那个弯，我们允许因为那儿太滑了。
You're cutting that corner, we allow
that because it's slippery there.

435
00:32:50,080 --> 00:32:51,160
哎呀！
Agh!

436
00:32:51,160 --> 00:32:56,120
有个铁血汉子。
快上，进去！
There is a man determined.
Go on, get in there!

437
00:32:56,120 --> 00:33:00,560
这已经是我见过的在倒数第二个弯里表现最好的了。
That is about as good
as I've ever seen
anyone do the second to last turn.

438
00:33:00,560 --> 00:33:03,959
进去！快啊！
Get in there! Come on!

439
00:33:07,679 --> 00:33:09,919
哦，不！
Oh, no!

440
00:33:09,919 --> 00:33:11,920
我受不了了！
I can't take it!

441
00:33:11,920 --> 00:33:18,919
你知道吗，
我昨天正坐在那里，
心里想：“明天得搞《Top Gear》。”
Do you know,
I was sitting there yesterday,
I thought, "Top Gear tomorrow."

442
00:33:18,919 --> 00:33:25,799
我在看《The Right Stuff》，
真的很喜欢，“去他妈的，赶紧上床，
确保精神爽利像朵雏菊。”
I'm watching The Right Stuff, which I
really enjoy, "Sod it, get to bed and
make sure you are fresh as a daisy."

443
00:33:25,799 --> 00:33:28,159
你昨晚早睡了？
我也早睡了，没错。
You had an early night?
I had an early night, yeah.

444
00:33:28,159 --> 00:33:31,360
那你有本事做到这事儿？
我当然有本事。
So you'd be capable of doing this?
So I would be capable of doing this.

445
00:33:31,360 --> 00:33:37,360
我手里这张纸
是制片给的
上面记着你们的九圈成绩。
What I've got here is a bit of paper
given to me by the producer
with all your nine laps.

446
00:33:37,360 --> 00:33:39,679
这东西不重要吧？
It isn't important, this, is it?

447
00:33:39,679 --> 00:33:45,760
还有更重要的
世界上正在发生的事！
这根本不重要。对吧？
There's more important
things going on in the world!
This is not important. Right.

448
00:33:45,760 --> 00:33:49,079
你这九圈里最快的一圈。
天啊，究竟是多少？
Your fastest lap of the nine.
Christ, what is it there?

449
00:33:49,079 --> 00:33:53,080
怎么回事？1分45.9秒。1分45.9秒。
What was he? 1:45.9. 1:45.9.

450
00:33:53,080 --> 00:33:56,879
拜托，真的吧？
你最快的那圈。
Come on, surely?
Your fastest lap.

451
00:33:56,879 --> 00:33:58,319
一...
One...

452
00:33:58,319 --> 00:34:03,800
我讨厌这个。我在看别人...
我本不该干这个。
I hate this. I watch other people...
I'm not supposed to be doing this.

453
00:34:03,800 --> 00:34:05,279
四十...哦！
forty... Oh!

454
00:34:05,279 --> 00:34:08,120
六点二...
six point two...

455
00:34:08,120 --> 00:34:09,400
啊——！
Agh!

456
00:34:10,480 --> 00:34:12,319
哔——！
BLEEP!

457
00:34:12,319 --> 00:34:16,199
这是你的第二...
最快的第二圈。
was your second...
was your second fastest lap.

458
00:34:16,199 --> 00:34:19,400
兴奋的咆哮
哔——！
EXCITED ROARS
BLEEP!

459
00:34:19,400 --> 00:34:22,559
你 哔——！
You BLEEP!

460
00:34:22,559 --> 00:34:24,519
哔——！
BLEEP!

461
00:34:29,360 --> 00:34:32,839
看，我只想说...
1分46.2秒是你的第二快。
Look, all I want to do...
1:46.2 was your second fastest.

462
00:34:32,839 --> 00:34:35,879
请让我...
你又拿了1分46.2秒。
Please let me...
You did another 1:46.2.

463
00:34:35,879 --> 00:34:39,760
1分48.2秒。1分49秒？！
1:48.2. 1:49?!

464
00:34:39,760 --> 00:34:42,359
那是我换错档的时候。
That was when I got the wrong gear.

465
00:34:42,359 --> 00:34:45,639
1分47秒，1分48秒。然后第八圈…
1:47, 1:48. Then on lap eight...

466
00:34:45,639 --> 00:34:51,280
这会是你的最快。
你得超过1分45.9秒。
That'll be your quickest.
You have 1:45.9 to beat.

467
00:34:51,280 --> 00:34:52,359
一…
One...

468
00:34:52,359 --> 00:34:54,400
四十…
forty...

469
00:34:54,400 --> 00:34:55,960
五…
five...

470
00:34:55,960 --> 00:34:57,479
点…
point...

471
00:34:58,480 --> 00:34:59,800
…八。
..eight.

472
00:34:59,800 --> 00:35:02,200
狂热掌声
WILD APPLAUSE

473
00:35:13,919 --> 00:35:16,359
来啊！来啊！
Come on! Come on!

474
00:35:17,840 --> 00:35:20,039
来啊！
Come on!

475
00:35:20,039 --> 00:35:22,720
干得好，兄弟。
Well, done, mate.

476
00:35:23,320 --> 00:35:27,280
女士们，先生们，
Jay Kay。全新第一名。
Ladies and gentlemen,
Jay Kay. The new number one.

477
00:35:34,040 --> 00:35:35,839
谢谢。
Thank you.

478
00:35:35,839 --> 00:35:37,640
成绩是1分45.81秒。
It was a 1:45.81.

479
00:35:37,640 --> 00:35:39,560
你可以把它带回家装框挂起来。
You can take that home and frame it.

480
00:35:42,160 --> 00:35:45,040
现在谁是老大？!
不是西蒙。
考威尔。
Who's the daddy now?!
Not Simon Cowell.

481
00:35:46,720 --> 00:35:52,280
所以我们又回到秋季了，我猜第一个嘉宾会是……西蒙·考尔。
So we are back in the autumn
and the first guest, I am
guessing will be...Simon Cowell.

482
00:35:52,280 --> 00:35:57,560
太棒了，女士们先生们，新晋第一名，杰伊·凯！
Brilliant. Ladies and gentlemen,
the new number one, Jay Kay!

483
00:35:57,560 --> 00:36:00,680
非常感谢。（观众欢呼）
Thank you very much.
CHEERING

484
00:36:05,360 --> 00:36:08,879
现在，德国有了一个全新的电视节目。
Now, there's a new
TV show in Germany.

485
00:36:08,879 --> 00:36:12,760
该节目全是关于汽车的，由三个人主持。
It's all about cars,
it is hosted by three people.

486
00:36:12,760 --> 00:36:14,759
我根本想不到他们是从哪儿冒出这个点子的，真是一头雾水。
I can't imagine where they
got that idea from, no idea.

487
00:36:17,360 --> 00:36:24,359
他们联系了我们，邀请我们在一系列赛跑和挑战中与他们一决高下。
They got in touch with us and
invited us to take them on in
a series of races and challenges.

488
00:36:24,359 --> 00:36:26,720
显然，我们得找个地方来搭台。
Obviously, we needed
somewhere to stage this.

489
00:36:26,720 --> 00:36:30,880
我提议在英格兰南部的上空搞。
I suggested in the skies
over southern England.

490
00:36:30,880 --> 00:36:35,079
事实上，我们最后选定了比利时，这个国家好像是专门为了让英国
In fact, we settled on Belgium,
a country invented so that Britain

491
00:36:35,079 --> 00:36:38,200
和德国有个地方可以把矛盾摆平。
and Germany would have somewhere
to sort out their differences.

492
00:36:38,200 --> 00:36:43,760
在这点上，制作人对我们说：“你们代表BBC，
On that point the producers told us,
"You are representing the BBC,

493
00:36:43,760 --> 00:36:46,720
‘不能随便出现，还要一直说战争的事。’”
"you can't just turn up
and go on about the war."

494
00:36:50,919 --> 00:36:57,359
这场会面定在上午9点，地点是比利时第二知名的赛道——佐尔德尔。
The meet was set for 9:00am
for Belgium's second
best-known race track, Zolder.

495
00:37:01,920 --> 00:37:08,720
恰好9点整，我们的德国朋友们开着炫目的德国车抵达。
And at precisely 9.00am,
our Germans arrived
in their impressive German cars.

496
00:37:17,759 --> 00:37:20,959
其实我们并没有迟到，只是帅气地到场而已。
In fact, we were not late,
we were simply arriving in style.

497
00:38:02,240 --> 00:38:04,799
来吧，Biggles！
Come on, Biggles!

498
00:38:08,399 --> 00:38:10,439
我们孤军作战，咱们……
We are on our own, we're...

499
00:38:10,439 --> 00:38:12,599
抢时间，时间不等人！
playing for time and
it is running out!

500
00:38:25,600 --> 00:38:27,879
我觉得我们可能玩过头了。
I think we might have overdone this.

501
00:38:27,879 --> 00:38:31,999
更糟的情况是，我们还可能排在鲍比·查尔顿的后面！
It could be worse,
we could have come in the back of
Bobby Charlton!

502
00:38:31,999 --> 00:38:35,440
杰里米。嗨，见到你很高兴，近来怎么样？
Jeremy. Hi. Good to see you.
How are you?

503
00:38:35,440 --> 00:38:41,399
我们闲聊倒是挺友好的，但说实话，还是有点紧张。
Our small talk was friendly, but,
to be honest, we were a bit nervous.

504
00:38:41,399 --> 00:38:43,880
当然，他们有个穿西装的欢脱家伙。
Sure, they had
a jolly man in a suit.

505
00:38:43,880 --> 00:38:49,799
他叫卡斯顿·冯·瑞森，根本没有赛车经验，
He is called Carston von Ryssen,
he has no racing experience at all,

506
00:38:49,799 --> 00:38:53,319
但他们还请来了旅行赛手蒂姆·施里克，
but then they also have
Tim Schrick, the touring driver

507
00:38:53,319 --> 00:38:57,680
以及纽博格林老手萨宾·施密茨。
and Sabine Schmitz,
the Nuerburgring specialist.

508
00:38:59,879 --> 00:39:03,280
他们要和我们一堆人对抗。
They were up against us lot.

509
00:39:03,280 --> 00:39:07,600
第一个挑战是德国人想出来的。
The first challenge was
dreamed up by the Germans.

510
00:39:07,600 --> 00:39:10,879
叫双层赛车，思路很简单。
It is called double decker
racing and the idea is simple.

511
00:39:10,879 --> 00:39:16,280
下面那辆车有油门、刹车和档位，但没有方向盘。
The car on the bottom has
a throttle, brakes and gears
but no steering wheel.

512
00:39:16,280 --> 00:39:19,879
因为方向盘装在上面的那辆车上。
because that is fitted
to the car on top.

513
00:39:19,879 --> 00:39:25,919
因为每边只有三位主持，但操作四辆车需要八个人，
Because there are only three
presenters on each side and
you need eight people to operate

514
00:39:25,919 --> 00:39:31,519
所以每队可以叫来摄制组的成员来帮忙。
the four cars, each team is allowed
to get someone from their film crew
to help out.

515
00:39:31,519 --> 00:39:34,080
这对德国人是个麻烦，因为虽然他们有
That is a problem for the Germans,
because, whilst they have

516
00:39:34,080 --> 00:39:38,639
一名录音师、一名摄像师和一名导演，但其实是同一个人。
a sound recordist, a cameraman
and a director, he is the same man.

517
00:39:38,639 --> 00:39:44,279
于是他们对这场比赛的拍摄只能是……
So their coverage of this race
is going to look like this...

518
00:39:44,279 --> 00:39:49,920
对我们来说也不怎么光彩，因为虽然我们摄制组很庞大，
But it is not that brilliant for
us, because, although we have
a very large film crew, there was

519
00:39:49,920 --> 00:39:56,720
但只有一个志愿者坐在我上面，说实话，这根本不是我想要的那位。
only one volunteer to sit above me
and, if I am honest, it is not
the one I would have picked.

520
00:39:56,720 --> 00:39:58,679
不过，他还是挺勇敢的。
Still, he is very brave.

521
00:39:58,679 --> 00:40:00,959
他曾经跟鲨鱼肉搏过。
He once fought a shark.

522
00:40:00,959 --> 00:40:03,040
虽然输给了它，不过算了！
He lost, but anyway!

523
00:40:04,759 --> 00:40:08,679
我们跑六圈，车身挂六条白条。
We do six laps
and have six white stripes.

524
00:40:08,679 --> 00:40:12,839
完成第一圈，就把一条减掉。
If you finish the first
one you take one off.

525
00:40:12,839 --> 00:40:18,240
詹姆斯，你能保证只踩油门不光踩刹车吗？
James, will you promise to use
the throttle and not just the brake?

526
00:40:18,240 --> 00:40:21,239
没有方向盘有点奇怪啊。
It's a bit odd
not having a steering wheel.

527
00:40:21,239 --> 00:40:25,240
这批Metro的方向盘手感不错，这招也算是个妙法。
These Metros have quite
good steering, so this is
a good way round to do it.

528
00:40:25,240 --> 00:40:27,599
没啥差别，你这傻逼。
It doesn't make
a difference, you idiot.

529
00:40:27,599 --> 00:40:30,559
方向是Metro在打，你在开Jag。
The steering is done by the Metro.
You're steering the Jag.

530
00:40:30,559 --> 00:40:33,040
好在车顶上装了高尔夫。
The good thing is that
they have Golfs on the roof.

531
00:40:33,040 --> 00:40:34,759
说实话，高尔夫这车挺重的。
Now, Golfs are heavy.

532
00:40:34,759 --> 00:40:37,360
Metro可是蛇皮材质的。
Metros are made out of snake skin.

533
00:40:40,280 --> 00:40:41,440
好了。
Right.

534
00:40:41,440 --> 00:40:42,640
开始啦。
Here we go.

535
00:40:44,560 --> 00:40:46,000
对！
Yes!

536
00:40:46,000 --> 00:40:47,559
稍等，杰里米。
Hang on, Jeremy.

537
00:40:50,360 --> 00:40:52,280
我们抢到了一个早起的领先！
We have got an early lead!

538
00:40:57,159 --> 00:40:58,840
我们已经掉到最后了！
We're already at the back!

539
00:41:04,880 --> 00:41:07,000
靠，这车要是不好好控制就要翻车了。
Jesus, that is going to roll over
if we are not careful.

540
00:41:09,440 --> 00:41:13,120
德国系统运转得很顺。
the German system was working well.

541
00:41:16,560 --> 00:41:18,119
而Metro车队那边…
Whereas in the Metro squadron...

542
00:41:18,119 --> 00:41:21,159
看你干啥呢，左转，左转。
Look at what
you are doing, left, left.

543
00:41:21,159 --> 00:41:23,999
左转！
Left!

544
00:41:23,999 --> 00:41:24,999
稳住！
Smooth!

545
00:41:26,000 --> 00:41:27,880
右！
Right!

546
00:41:27,880 --> 00:41:31,480
然后通讯彻底崩溃了。
Then there was
a complete communication breakdown.

547
00:41:39,039 --> 00:41:40,480
哇哦！左，左，左！
Whoa! Left, left, left!

548
00:41:40,480 --> 00:41:43,559
德国小子们已经占到第一、第二了。
The Germans
were now first and second.

549
00:41:45,800 --> 00:41:48,039
这简直是灾难！
This is a disaster!

550
00:41:48,039 --> 00:41:51,760
接着又出事了，我的“翼手”们疯了。
Then there was another one.
My wing men went mad.

551
00:41:51,760 --> 00:41:54,800
里侧。
On the inside.

552
00:41:54,800 --> 00:41:58,679
不。不。不！你到底干了啥？
No. No. No! What the hell
have you done that for?

553
00:42:03,640 --> 00:42:07,400
那是你不好。你是他妈的方向盘手！
That was your fault.
You're on the bloody steering!

554
00:42:07,400 --> 00:42:09,680
詹姆斯和理查德觉得完蛋了，他们说得对！
James and Richard think
it's all over, and they're right!

555
00:42:12,239 --> 00:42:15,519
垃圾，你把车给拐进了碎石里，那是用来拦停F1赛车的。
Rubbish, you steered into
the gravel it is designed
to stop Formula One cars.

556
00:42:15,519 --> 00:42:20,080
你到底怎么想的，Jaguar车顶上挂个Metro…
How the hell do you think a
Jaguar with a Metro on its roof...

557
00:42:20,080 --> 00:42:22,960
这简直是我们最黑暗的时刻。
This was our darkest hour.

558
00:42:22,960 --> 00:42:25,600
我们被碾碎了。
We are being annihilated.

559
00:42:25,600 --> 00:42:31,239
只剩我们掉线，只能祈祷杰里米和音效师Kipp能公平干净地比赛。
With us out, we could only hope that
Jeremy and Kipp the sound man would
race on cleanly and fairly.

560
00:42:31,239 --> 00:42:33,400
撞他，撞！
Ram him. Ram!

561
00:42:34,280 --> 00:42:36,400
上吧，Kipp。
Go, Kipp.

562
00:42:37,319 --> 00:42:39,640
是啊，他们已经搞砸了。我们搞定他们。
Yes, they've gone wrong.
We got them.

563
00:42:39,640 --> 00:42:44,479
刚刚离开，他已经出局。
just off, he was out.

564
00:42:46,119 --> 00:42:49,640
现在只剩我们对阵Sabine和那位西装男。
Now it was just us versus Sabine
and a man in a suit.

565
00:42:52,760 --> 00:42:55,760
快点！根本没有护航战斗机。
Come on! There's no fighter escort.

566
00:42:59,000 --> 00:43:00,999
往里线冲，baff，没错！
Up the inside, baff, yes!

567
00:43:02,560 --> 00:43:04,720
上吧，Kipp。他们掉下来了！
Go, Kipp. They've gone down!

568
00:43:13,559 --> 00:43:18,559
想在《Top Gear》上为国家和工作争光，Kipp干了一件大胆事。
Keen to defend his country
and his job on Top Gear,
Kipp made a bold move.

569
00:43:21,760 --> 00:43:24,359
这给他们留点儿思考的余地。
That is giving them
something to think about.

570
00:43:24,359 --> 00:43:27,040
这也给了我们点儿思考的空间。
It also gave us
something to think about.

571
00:43:27,040 --> 00:43:30,800
Jeremy，我的手臂脱了！
Jeremy, my arm's come off!

572
00:43:30,800 --> 00:43:32,759
我的手臂脱了！
My arm's come off!

573
00:43:32,759 --> 00:43:36,440
赛车里从来没人这么说过！
Nobody has ever said that
in a car race before!

574
00:43:39,160 --> 00:43:41,200
我们已经进入最后一圈。
We were now on the last lap.

575
00:43:41,200 --> 00:43:43,520
在内线。
On the inside.

576
00:43:53,360 --> 00:43:55,239
现在真的挺难的，Jeremy。
It is quite difficult now, Jeremy.

577
00:43:59,559 --> 00:44:02,639
哦不，已经到终点了。不要——不要！
Oh, no, it is the finish.
No, No!

578
00:44:02,639 --> 00:44:03,879
不要！
No!

579
00:44:05,960 --> 00:44:09,760
我让英国丢脸了，哦不！
I've let Britain down, oh, no!

580
00:44:09,760 --> 00:44:15,080
希望下一个挑战能帮我们翻身。
Hopefully, we could redeem ourselves
in the next challenge.

581
00:44:18,599 --> 00:44:20,560
谁造的车最快？
Who makes the fastest cars?

582
00:44:20,560 --> 00:44:24,160
轴心国还是盟军？这点子是你想出来的吧？
The axis powers or the allies? You
came up with this one, didn't you?

583
00:44:24,160 --> 00:44:26,639
是啊。你根本没想清楚，对吧？
Yes. You haven't thought
it through, have you?

584
00:44:26,639 --> 00:44:28,919
我想过。简直天才简单——直线加速赛。
I did. It is brilliantly simple.
A drag race.

585
00:44:28,919 --> 00:44:30,680
来看看参赛选手吧。
Let's meet the contenders.

586
00:44:30,680 --> 00:44:34,960
德国这边，超级改装的保时捷9FF。
On their side from Germany,
the highly modified Porsche 9FF.

587
00:44:34,960 --> 00:44:37,840
意大利方面，兰博基尼。
From Italy, the Lamborghini.

588
00:44:37,840 --> 00:44:39,640
是LP640版。
That's the LP640 version.

589
00:44:39,640 --> 00:44:44,759
日本方面，三菱Evo 10，也就是FD360。
From Japan, the Mitsubishi
Evo 10, that's the FD360.

590
00:44:44,759 --> 00:44:46,599
是的，原本是他们的，现在归我们了。
Yes, that's there's, now ours.

591
00:44:46,599 --> 00:44:49,640
英格兰这边，由“飞行上尉”巴尼·哈蒙德驾驶，
From England and driven by
Wing Commander Bunny Hammond,

592
00:44:49,640 --> 00:44:52,320
这台阿里尔Atom，增压版。
is the Ariel Atom,
the supercharged version.

593
00:44:52,320 --> 00:44:57,959
再说美国，我想到了这里的这位下士——Callaway改装的科尔维特，同样是增压的。
Then from America, I was thinking
of you here, corporal, is the
Callaway Corvette, also supercharged.

594
00:44:57,959 --> 00:45:01,240
就像我说的，你根本没想清楚，对吧？
And like I was saying, you haven't
thought it through, have you?

595
00:45:01,240 --> 00:45:07,960
让我猜猜，James，新西兰竟然有辆V16火箭车我们竟然不知道？根本没有。
Let me guess, James, New Zealand
makes a V16 rocket car that somehow
we don't know about. They don't.

596
00:45:07,960 --> 00:45:13,400
不过，印度站在我们这边，我在等他们的车时，
However, India was on our side,
whilst I waited for one of their cars

597
00:45:13,400 --> 00:45:18,720
等它出现，我把其他人派去抹掉那台时速250英里的保时捷。
to turn up I sent the others
off to neuter the 250mph Porsche.

598
00:45:18,720 --> 00:45:29,639
他们说它起步时很难把那千马力全部释放出来。
And they decided it would
have trouble putting its 1000
horsepower down off the line.

599
00:45:29,639 --> 00:45:33,440
如果赛程只有四分之一英里，它就只能在这里原地打转。没错。
If the race is quarter of a mile
this is still gonna be sitting
here spinning its wheels. Yeah.

600
00:45:33,440 --> 00:45:35,120
对，保准你们会爱上这场面。
Right, you're gonna love this.

601
00:45:35,120 --> 00:45:38,200
这里有规章制度——你这类人就爱这玩意儿——
There are rules and regulations
- you like that sort of thing -

602
00:45:38,200 --> 00:45:41,680
关于直线加速赛，它们永远都是四分之一英里。
concerning a drag race, and they
are always a quarter of a mile.

603
00:45:41,680 --> 00:45:47,120
不，不。我们是用公里的，至少一公里。
No, no. We drive kilometres.
At least one kilometre.

604
00:45:47,120 --> 00:45:51,440
说到四分之一英里，大家都懂，那是标准数值。
If you say a quarter of a mile
everybody knows what that is
because it's the standard measure.

605
00:45:51,440 --> 00:45:53,319
来个半公里汉堡？算了吧。
Half kilometre burger, please, no.

606
00:45:53,319 --> 00:45:57,120
那是四分之一磅的汉堡，你却在跑四分之一英里加速赛。
It's a quarter pounder, you have
a quarter-mile drag race.

607
00:45:57,120 --> 00:45:59,279
这就是英国风格，干吧。
It's the British way. Let's do it.

608
00:46:00,400 --> 00:46:05,080
把9FF甩开后，我的注意力转向兰博基尼。
With the 9FF hopefully out of it my
attention turned to the Lamborghini.

609
00:46:07,640 --> 00:46:12,479
我只祈祷它这意大利货能在中途换挡。
What I'm hoping,
praying is that being Italian
it changes sides halfway down.

610
00:46:13,919 --> 00:46:17,800
我们准备时，詹姆斯的印度车终于出现了。
As we got ready, James's Indian car
finally turned up.

611
00:46:17,800 --> 00:46:20,560
超级增压。超级增压。
Supercharged. Supercharged.

612
00:46:20,560 --> 00:46:22,319
增压。
Charged.

613
00:46:34,319 --> 00:46:37,760
詹姆斯，别忘了关掉牵引力控制，兄弟。
James, don't forget to turn
your traction control off, mate.

614
00:46:40,159 --> 00:46:44,639
哎呀，我想起澳洲人了，他们玩那套VXR。
Cock. I've just remembered the
Australians. They do that VXR thing.

615
00:46:48,800 --> 00:46:51,680
高傲的哈蒙德抢了个闪电式起步。
Lofty Hammond got a lightning start.

616
00:46:51,800 --> 00:46:51,920
高傲的哈蒙德抢了个闪电式起步。
Lofty Hammond got a lightning start.

617
00:46:55,600 --> 00:46:58,400
这加速简直惊人！
This is unbelievable acceleration!

618
00:47:00,160 --> 00:47:04,679
《Atom》里的那颗原子肯定会赢，那谁会拿第二？
The atom in the Atom would clearly
win but who would come second?

619
00:47:04,679 --> 00:47:06,560
来啊！来啊！
Come on! Come on!

620
00:47:09,680 --> 00:47:14,279
兰博基尼把我弄晕了，但我能挡住那只怪兽保时捷吗？
The Lambo's got me. But could I
hold off that monstrous Porsche?

621
00:47:16,880 --> 00:47:18,200
可以！
Yes!

622
00:47:21,479 --> 00:47:24,920
是啊，那是我们的！是我们的！
Yeah, that is ours! That is ours!

623
00:47:28,720 --> 00:47:32,879
那…现在感觉咋样？
So...how do you feel now?

624
00:47:36,280 --> 00:47:41,639
我们拿了第一。再说一遍，明确——第一。
So we were first. Let's just say
that again, make it clear - first.

625
00:47:41,639 --> 00:47:45,280
第一。第三。第一。还有最后。
First. Third.
First. And last.

626
00:47:45,280 --> 00:47:49,880
好，你说最后，这也对称——我们有第一
Well, you say last. There's
a symmetry to that - we had first

627
00:47:49,880 --> 00:47:55,439
和最后，直线赛的两个关键位置被我们占据。我们把全场都给占了。
and last, the two most significant
places in the drag race are owned
by us. We own the whole territory.

628
00:47:55,439 --> 00:48:01,040
你们赢了双层巴士赛，我们得了点积分回来了。
You won the double deckers,
we've got some points back.

629
00:48:01,040 --> 00:48:03,599
直线赛标志着团队挑战结束。
The drag race marks
the end of the team challenges.

630
00:48:03,599 --> 00:48:06,479
从现在起，只剩一对一了。
From now on, it would be one-on-one.

631
00:48:09,799 --> 00:48:14,759
本次活动德国将派出赛道女王、赛车手萨宾娜·施密茨。
For this event Germany will be
represented by ring mistress,
racing driver, Sabine Schmitz.

632
00:48:14,759 --> 00:48:17,920
我们就是这么代表的。
We will be represented by that.

633
00:48:19,400 --> 00:48:25,240
不管怎样，车辆——每支队必须带一辆小巧、价位合理、来自本国的车。
Anyway, the cars - each team must
bring something small, reasonably
priced and from their own country.

634
00:48:25,240 --> 00:48:28,600
于是我们想到这——一台Mini Cooper S。
So we've come up with this -
it's a Mini Cooper S.

635
00:48:28,600 --> 00:48:31,079
萨宾娜，你带了啥？
Sabine, what have you got?

636
00:48:31,079 --> 00:48:33,280
我带的是那车。什么，高尔夫？
I've got that car. What, the Golf?

637
00:48:33,280 --> 00:48:36,039
不，是Mini Cooper，当然啦！
No, the Mini Cooper, of course!

638
00:48:36,039 --> 00:48:38,560
你没听啊？那是德国的。我们说了要本国的车。
Weren't you listening? It's German.
We said it's from your own country.

639
00:48:38,560 --> 00:48:41,159
就是Mini。
It's a Mini.

640
00:48:41,159 --> 00:48:45,280
再英国的车也没有Mini更英国！
You can't get more
British than a Mini!

641
00:48:45,280 --> 00:48:49,959
Alec Issigonis，这个名字还能  
更英国一点儿吗  
比 Issigonis 更？
Alec Issigonis, how much more
of a British name is there
than Issigonis?

642
00:48:49,959 --> 00:48:53,360
除了 Patel？全是英国味，英国味，英国味！
Apart from Patel?
British, British, British!

643
00:48:53,360 --> 00:48:56,279
好啊，我们坐的是同一款车。让他们上场吧。
OK, so we're in the same cars.
Just let them do it.

644
00:48:56,279 --> 00:49:02,519
于是来了国际小车挑战，规则如下……
So the International Small Car
Challenge, and it goes like this...

645
00:49:05,280 --> 00:49:09,359
在明代花瓶间穿梭。转向轻松得玩儿。
Slalom through the Ming vases.
Steering is so easy.

646
00:49:11,040 --> 00:49:14,399
倒车进那价值连城的陶瓷仓库。
Reverse into the garage
of priceless crockery.

647
00:49:14,399 --> 00:49:20,320
然后来个 J 弯罚分，偏偏德国选手竟然给漏了。
Then take a J turn penalty which,
amazingly, the German missed.

648
00:49:22,160 --> 00:49:25,079
接下来，打个八字形，期间
Next, drive a figure of eight
while a member of

649
00:49:25,079 --> 00:49:28,079
对手队员向你射击
the other team shoots at you

650
00:49:28,079 --> 00:49:31,319
来自一辆喷漆弹坦克。每中一次扣一分，逃离竞技场
from a paintball tank. One point
off for each hit, escape the arena

651
00:49:31,319 --> 00:49:34,480
穿过我们叫“迪克”的隧道。
through a tunnel we shall call Dick.

652
00:49:37,679 --> 00:49:41,399
但接下来轮到杰里米了。好运！
But then it was Jeremy's turn.
Gut luck.

653
00:49:41,399 --> 00:49:43,719
来了！
Here we go!

654
00:49:46,599 --> 00:49:49,760
到目前为止，一弹未中！
So far not one hit!

655
00:49:52,040 --> 00:49:53,999
这才对味儿。
That's the ticket.

656
00:49:55,600 --> 00:49:58,760
不过，后面还能更刺激。
Still, things could only get better.

657
00:50:01,119 --> 00:50:03,080
噢！我得分了。
Oh! I've scored.

658
00:50:03,080 --> 00:50:06,479
我只能靠八字形来挽回面子。
I only had the figure of eight
to redeem myself.

659
00:50:06,479 --> 00:50:08,000
来吧，手刹！
Come on, handbrake.

660
00:50:08,000 --> 00:50:09,119
开火！
Fire!

661
00:50:11,319 --> 00:50:12,359
开火！
Fire!

662
00:50:12,359 --> 00:50:17,080
这儿子弹打得我满身都是，怪不得。
An awful lot of bullets hitting me
here. And no wonder.

663
00:50:17,080 --> 00:50:20,399
詹姆斯！你干嘛呢？向杰里米开枪！
James! What are you doing?
Shooting at Jeremy.

664
00:50:20,399 --> 00:50:24,039
好啊，他是我们这边的！对呀，但你怎么会不这么干？你说得对！你会的！开火！
Well, he's on our side!
Yeah, but why wouldn't you?
You're right! You would! Fire!

665
00:50:29,000 --> 00:50:30,360
来呀，穿过迪克！
Come on, through Dick!

666
00:50:31,760 --> 00:50:35,879
是啊，连这都出错了。
Yes. Even that went wrong.

667
00:50:38,359 --> 00:50:41,279
所以，我在积分上落后。
So, I was trailing on points.

668
00:50:41,279 --> 00:50:45,719
但我还能在挑战的最后环节，正面对决里抢回分数
But I could win some back in
the final part of the challenge,
the head to head one

669
00:50:45,719 --> 00:50:52,400
在 Zolder 环道进行单圈赛，谁先把毛巾铺在日光浴床上谁就赢。
lap race around the Zolder circuit,
the winner would be the first one
to get their towel on the sunbed.

670
00:50:52,400 --> 00:50:54,760
与命运的约会。
A date with destiny.

671
00:50:59,440 --> 00:51:01,360
她领先的距离，她会说是一米。
She's ahead by what
she'd call a metre.

672
00:51:03,959 --> 00:51:05,240
嗨呀！
Woo!

673
00:51:11,279 --> 00:51:14,399
她早早抢到前面，我可
She's breaking early there, I'm not

674
00:51:14,399 --> 00:51:17,200
不想这么干，我立马冲进去。
going to do that.
I dive down inside.

675
00:51:17,200 --> 00:51:19,599
我领先啦！
I'm in the lead!

676
00:51:19,599 --> 00:51:21,520
我才不是领先！
I'm not in the lead!

677
00:51:30,160 --> 00:51:34,479
电视蠢货想尽办法想超车。
The TV idiot was trying
everything to get past.

678
00:51:44,320 --> 00:51:49,840
来呀！杰里米！这才算是真正的比赛。
Come on! Jeremy!
This really was a proper race.

679
00:51:50,999 --> 00:51:53,000
我不废话，这事儿重要。
I'm not talking, this matters.

680
00:52:03,640 --> 00:52:06,200
杰里米，给他一次说对的机会吧。
Jeremy, let him get something right.

681
00:52:08,279 --> 00:52:10,319
不行！不行！不行！
No! No! No!

682
00:52:10,319 --> 00:52:13,479
他们得冲到桥上去。
They've got to get up to the bridge.

683
00:52:18,639 --> 00:52:23,079
在这种环境下，根本不可能打败德国人。
There's no possibility, in this
environment, of beating a German.

684
00:52:23,079 --> 00:52:24,839
那真是软弱。然后你又没……
That was feeble.
And then you didn't...

685
00:52:24,839 --> 00:52:28,839
抱歉。你在向那辆坦克开火吗？是的，他是这么干的。
Sorry. Were you shooting at me? In
that tank? He was, yes, he did that.

686
00:52:30,439 --> 00:52:34,840
那场闹剧后，我们落后了九分。
After that debacle,
we were trailing by nine points.

687
00:52:38,119 --> 00:52:43,480
但我正要迎接下一个挑战，而这次是一场在我这类车里的对决。
But I was handling the next
challenge. And it was to be
a shoot-out in my kind of car.

688
00:52:43,480 --> 00:52:46,119
这台令人惊叹的 Bowler Nemesis。
The incredible Bowler Nemesis.

689
00:52:46,119 --> 00:52:50,439
4.4 升 V8，300 马力，0-60 英里/时加速六秒。
4.4 litre V8, 300 brake horse
power, 0 to 60 in six seconds.

690
00:52:50,439 --> 00:52:53,039
最高时速 130 英里/小时。
Top speed 130 miles an hour.

691
00:52:53,039 --> 00:52:57,040
但一如既往，Bowler 这玩意能在任何地方、任何路面上做到。
But, as always, with a Bowler,
it can do that anywhere on anything.

692
00:52:57,040 --> 00:53:01,040
更妙的是，我的对手居然是会计。
And better still,
my opponent would be the accountant.

693
00:53:01,040 --> 00:53:03,640
开过 Bowler？没有。好啊。
Driven a Bowler before? No. Good.

694
00:53:03,640 --> 00:53:06,719
好。呃，它们真吓人。
Good. Well, they're terrifying.

695
00:53:06,719 --> 00:53:10,480
他根本不赛车吗？不，从来不赛，他根本没有车。
Does he not do any racing?
No, never, he hasn't got a car.

696
00:53:10,480 --> 00:53:12,719
没有。他只有个驾照，仅此而已。
No. He has a licence, that's it.

697
00:53:12,719 --> 00:53:17,799
有位司机开太快，肺都给震出来了。
One driver dislodged
his lung when he went too fast.

698
00:53:17,799 --> 00:53:20,120
但你会没事的，肯定玩得爽。祝好运。
But you'll be fine,
you'll enjoy this. Good luck.

699
00:53:20,120 --> 00:53:27,479
这是一场五圈赛，赛道约60%是柏油，另外多亏詹姆斯，竟然还有60%是碎石。
It would be a five lap race over
a track that was 60% Tarmac and,
thanks to James, 60% gravel.

700
00:53:39,479 --> 00:53:41,519
我们起跑了。来吧，强大的 Bowler。
We are off. Come on, mighty Bowler.

701
00:53:47,600 --> 00:53:53,440
在柏油路上，会计还能跟上，但一到泥地，他根本看不见我这尘土飞扬的身影。
On Tarmac, the accountant kept up,
but once we hit the dirt,
he wouldn't see me for dust.

702
00:53:55,199 --> 00:53:58,160
没错！正是如此！
Yes! More like it!

703
00:53:58,160 --> 00:54:00,480
与此同时，基地那边……
Meanwhile, back at base...

704
00:54:00,480 --> 00:54:02,960
坐下。
Sit down.

705
00:54:02,960 --> 00:54:05,879
你对这些一点也不感兴趣，是吧？
You're not
interested in these, are you?

706
00:54:05,879 --> 00:54:11,960
你知道吗？你的脑子根本无法理解我对这些事儿有多不在乎。
Do you know what? Your mind cannot
comprehend of how uninterested
I am in things like this.

707
00:54:15,999 --> 00:54:19,040
回到赛道，哈蒙德甭想甩掉那位西装男的尾巴。
Back on track,
Hammond couldn't shake
the man in the suit off his tail.

708
00:54:19,040 --> 00:54:22,240
他显然是个值得敬佩的对手。
He was clearly a worthy adversary.

709
00:54:23,559 --> 00:54:25,400
保持脚在哈蒙德的车上，胆子大点。
Keep your foot in Hammond, be brave.

710
00:54:31,919 --> 00:54:35,399
哈蒙德就在稍后证明了这一点。
A point Hammond
proved, moments later.

711
00:54:42,360 --> 00:54:44,359
他笑了
HE LAUGHS

712
00:54:46,199 --> 00:54:51,200
要是你们搞不动这个，哈蒙德，对我们来说，竞争就结束了！
If you don't get that going,
Hammond, for us,
ze competition is over!

713
00:54:51,200 --> 00:54:52,760
那下场可不妙啊。
That didn't go well, then.

714
00:54:52,760 --> 00:54:55,480
这是一场必须夺冠的比赛。
This was a race we had to win.

715
00:54:55,480 --> 00:54:58,599
可增值税那位哥们已经遥遥领先。
But the VAT man had a big lead.

716
00:54:58,599 --> 00:55:01,160
我马上要挨骂了，这可不妙。
I'm going to get grief
for this, now, this is not good.

717
00:55:01,160 --> 00:55:02,840
凉快了！八周！
Cooler! Eight weeks!

718
00:55:07,519 --> 00:55:09,159
赛道哪儿跑了？
Where's the track gone?

719
00:55:12,280 --> 00:55:13,960
他在加速吗？正在加速。
Is he gaining? He is gaining.

720
00:55:31,040 --> 00:55:35,000
在最后一个弯，我决定在外侧超他。
On the last corner, I decided
to take him on the outside.

721
00:55:35,000 --> 00:55:37,479
我把他叫过来！
I can have him here!

722
00:55:41,999 --> 00:55:43,719
好啊！
Yes!

723
00:55:44,440 --> 00:55:46,399
耶！
Yeah!

724
00:55:46,399 --> 00:55:48,639
干得好。谢谢！
Well done, then. Thank you!

725
00:55:48,639 --> 00:55:53,720
你知道烂输家是什么吗？
哈蒙德就是所谓的烂赢家。
You know what a bad loser is?
Well, Hammond is what's called
a bad winner.

726
00:55:53,720 --> 00:55:56,439
是的！
YES!

727
00:55:58,040 --> 00:55:59,999
你怎么看？
What do you think of that?

728
00:56:02,159 --> 00:56:05,000
那就恭喜我吧，我赢了。你注意到我第一名了吗？
Congratulate me, then, I've won.
Did you notice, I was first?

729
00:56:05,000 --> 00:56:10,759
哈蒙德那点小胜之后，我们
只落后四分
After Hammond's modest win, we
were trailing by just four points

730
00:56:10,759 --> 00:56:13,600
进入最后一项时。
as we went into the last event.

731
00:56:13,600 --> 00:56:17,000
这是佐尔德赛道的两圈赛。
It's a two-lap race
of the Zolder circuit.

732
00:56:17,000 --> 00:56:21,800
一辆保时捷911，对手是一辆赛车版保时捷911，由
It's between a Porsche 911, a racing
Porsche 911, which will be driven by

733
00:56:21,800 --> 00:56:24,280
职业赛车手蒂姆·施里克驾驶。
professional racing driver,
Tim Schrick.

734
00:56:24,280 --> 00:56:31,760
而他将对阵一辆阿斯顿·马丁DBRS9，
由詹姆斯·梅驾驶。
And he will be against
an Aston Martin DBRS9,
which will be driven by James May.

735
00:56:31,760 --> 00:56:34,760
难道非得让詹姆斯上吗？
Do we have to use James?

736
00:56:34,760 --> 00:56:36,999
好吧，不是的，你搞了个Bowler，我搞了个Mini，现在轮到他了。
Well, no, you did the Bowler thing,
I did the Mini thing, it's his turn.

737
00:56:36,999 --> 00:56:39,280
不过，他会输得很惨的。
But, he's going to lose, badly.

738
00:56:39,280 --> 00:56:44,000
倒是我想到了个计划。
Happily, though,
I'd come up with a plan.

739
00:56:44,000 --> 00:56:47,600
懂我意思吧？聪明。非常聪明。
You know what I mean?
Clever. Very clever.

740
00:56:51,640 --> 00:56:55,559
是詹姆斯。是詹姆斯，对，他来参加比赛了。他
总是……总是穿成这副样子。
It's James. It's James, yeah,
he's come in for the race. He
always...always dresses like this.

741
00:56:55,559 --> 00:56:58,799
但这到底是啥？
But what is this?

742
00:56:58,799 --> 00:57:01,560
他开赛车时总是这么穿。祝好运。
He always dresses like this when
he drives a racing car. Good luck.

743
00:57:01,560 --> 00:57:04,160
谁给他剪的头？
Who cut his hair?

744
00:57:04,160 --> 00:57:05,879
他脑子不正常。
He's lost it.

745
00:57:05,879 --> 00:57:09,119
别打扰他专注的状态，他正进入比赛的状态。
Don't disturb him when he's focused
and in his zone, ready for a race.

746
00:57:09,119 --> 00:57:12,719
他冷静得像块冰。好，这招也许行得通。
He's ice-cool. Well, this could work.

747
00:57:12,719 --> 00:57:15,399
可以的。机会很大。
Could do. There's every chance.

748
00:57:15,399 --> 00:57:17,639
会是滚动式起跑。
It would be a rolling start.

749
00:57:17,639 --> 00:57:21,799
因为我们落后四分，詹姆斯正热着轮胎，
Because we were four points behind,
James, who's warming his tyres up,

750
00:57:21,799 --> 00:57:25,840
必须在保时捷之后四秒起步。
had to set off four seconds
after the Porsche.

751
00:57:31,359 --> 00:57:33,319
比赛开始了。
The race was on.

752
00:57:34,919 --> 00:57:37,840
加油，詹姆斯！冲啊！
Go, James! Go!

753
00:57:44,960 --> 00:57:47,920
说白了就是这么回事，我们这小子得抢占
The simple fact of the matter
is this, our young man had to shoot

754
00:57:47,920 --> 00:57:53,840
把那小子甩开，每圈差两秒。
down their young man
at the rate of two seconds a lap.

755
00:58:05,759 --> 00:58:08,959
如果他在直道全开油门，根本甩不慢。
If he does full throttle on
the straight, it's not kept slow.

756
00:58:08,959 --> 00:58:14,400
我知道……那是他的绰号，你懂吧？
I know...
That's his nickname, you know?

757
00:58:14,400 --> 00:58:16,280
我们叫他‘高个子’，恰恰相反。
We call him Lofty.
It's the opposite.

758
00:58:18,800 --> 00:58:24,119
第一圈快结束时，詹姆斯把差距缩小到只有一秒。
Towards the end of the first lap,
James had closed the gap
to just one second.

759
00:58:36,359 --> 00:58:40,600
詹姆斯开得精彩，却不幸出事。
James was driving brilliantly
but then disaster.

760
00:58:40,600 --> 00:58:46,279
他刹车锁死，失去优势，只能重新来一遍。
He locked up, he lost ground, he had
the work to do all over again.

761
00:58:50,480 --> 00:58:52,519
好啦，詹姆斯可不是那种半路就拔腿就跑的家伙。
Happily, James is no quitter.

762
00:58:52,519 --> 00:58:56,960
还剩半圈时，他又回到了保时捷的尾流里。
With half a lap to go, he was
right back under the Porsche's wing.

763
00:59:03,640 --> 00:59:07,360
只剩两个弯了，他抓住机会发动冲刺。
With just two corners to go,
he made his move.

764
00:59:09,320 --> 00:59:12,599
~ 我不想看！我听到了，两边的声音都听得到！
I don't want to see! I can
hear them, I can hear them both!

765
00:59:12,599 --> 00:59:15,359
哪辆车会先冲出来？
Which car would appear first?

766
00:59:15,359 --> 00:59:18,680
哪一辆？
Which one?

767
00:59:20,159 --> 00:59:21,959
它出来了！
It's there!

768
00:59:21,959 --> 00:59:23,440
斯提格！詹姆斯！
Stig! James!

769
00:59:23,440 --> 00:59:26,400
CHEERING
CHEERING

770
00:59:31,960 --> 00:59:34,400
詹姆斯。
James.

771
00:59:36,120 --> 00:59:37,959
詹姆斯。
James.

772
00:59:37,959 --> 00:59:40,920
有人说，你救了我们的命。
Some say, you saved our bacon.

773
00:59:40,920 --> 00:59:43,719
还有人说，我在更衣室被捆住，嘴巴被塞住。
Others say I was bound
and gagged in the locker room.

774
00:59:43,719 --> 00:59:45,319
LAUGHTER
LAUGHTER

775
00:59:45,319 --> 00:59:49,079
说到那颗弹跳炸弹，现在是收场的时候了。
And on that bouncing bomb shell,
it's now time to end.

776
00:59:49,079 --> 00:59:55,719
如果你是德国人，对这部电影有任何不满，随时写信给我们。
If you are a German and you have
any complaints about the film you've
seen, do feel free to write to us.

777
00:59:55,719 --> 00:59:59,519
我们的地址是，1966
Our address is, 1966

778
00:59:59,519 --> 01:00:04,319
埃尔阿拉曼广场，1939至1945日德兰街，伦敦，
El Alamein Square, 1939
to 1945 Jutland Street, London,

779
01:00:04,319 --> 01:00:06,880
WE1!
WE1!

780
01:00:06,880 --> 01:00:09,880
CHEERING
CHEERING

781
01:00:09,880 --> 01:00:12,520
秋天见。感谢收看，保重，晚安！
See you in the autumn. Thanks for
watching. Take care. Good night!

782
01:00:12,520 --> 01:00:15,960
CHEERING
CHEERING

